1
00:00:35,547 --> 00:00:37,299
Young people from all over the globe...

2
00:00:37,387 --> 00:00:39,378
are joining up
to fight for the future.

3
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:42,186
- I'm doing my part.
- I'm doing my part.

4
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:45,703
- I'm doing my part.
- I'm doing my part too.

5
00:00:47,587 --> 00:00:49,657
They're doing their part,
are you?

6
00:00:49,747 --> 00:00:52,136
Join the Mobile Infantry
and save the world.

7
00:00:52,227 --> 00:00:54,616
Service guarantees citizenship.

8
00:00:58,387 --> 00:01:01,299
The bugs send
another meteor our way...

9
00:01:01,387 --> 00:01:03,105
but this time we're ready.

10
00:01:03,187 --> 00:01:06,497
Planetary defences
are better than ever.

11
00:01:10,947 --> 00:01:13,415
Klendathu, source
of the bug meteor attacks...

12
00:01:13,507 --> 00:01:16,783
orbits a twin star system whose
brutal gravitational forces...

13
00:01:16,867 --> 00:01:19,779
produce an unlimited supply
of bug meteorites...

14
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:22,381
in the form
of this asteroid belt.

15
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:24,617
To ensure the safety
of our solar system...

16
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:27,096
Klendathu
must be eliminated.

17
00:01:28,547 --> 00:01:31,186
We break net now and take you
live to Klendathu...

18
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:33,906
where the invasion
has begun.

19
00:01:33,987 --> 00:01:37,263
EXQ uplink on two, one.
You're on.

20
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:39,815
- We'vejust landed here
on what cap troopers...
- Move, move, move!

21
00:01:39,907 --> 00:01:41,898
- are calling Big K,
- Come on! Move, move!

22
00:01:41,987 --> 00:01:44,455
- with the 6th Mobile Infantry Division!
- Come on!

23
00:01:44,547 --> 00:01:47,664
It's an ugly planet,
a bug planet!

24
00:01:47,747 --> 00:01:50,341
A planet hostile to life
as we know it!

25
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:54,986
Help me!

26
00:02:05,587 --> 00:02:08,260
- Come on! Go, go, go!
- Keep moving!

27
00:02:08,347 --> 00:02:09,939
Get out of here now!

28
00:02:18,907 --> 00:02:20,420
Kitten, no!

29
00:02:30,587 --> 00:02:31,906
Oh, God!

30
00:02:32,907 --> 00:02:34,022
Oh, God!

31
00:02:48,507 --> 00:02:53,103
Rico. Rico. Rico!

32
00:02:56,307 --> 00:02:58,104
Pay attention.

33
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:00,784
Sorry, Mr Rasczak.

34
00:03:00,867 --> 00:03:02,823
Let's sum up.

35
00:03:02,907 --> 00:03:05,580
This year we explored
the failure of democracy...

36
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:07,385
- Bad boy.
- how the social scientists
brought our world...

37
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:09,219
to the brink of chaos.

38
00:03:09,307 --> 00:03:11,946
We talked about the veterans,
how they took control...

39
00:03:12,027 --> 00:03:16,145
and imposed the stability
that has lasted for generations since.

40
00:03:16,227 --> 00:03:17,945
You know these facts...

41
00:03:18,027 --> 00:03:20,257
but have I taught you anything
of value this year?

42
00:03:20,347 --> 00:03:21,826
Hmm?

43
00:03:21,907 --> 00:03:23,784
You. Why are only citizens
allowed to vote?

44
00:03:23,867 --> 00:03:25,300
It's a reward,

45
00:03:25,387 --> 00:03:28,026
what the Federation gives you
for doing Federal Service.

46
00:03:28,107 --> 00:03:30,177
No. No.

47
00:03:30,267 --> 00:03:33,623
Something given
has no value.

48
00:03:33,707 --> 00:03:36,858
Look, when you vote, you are
exercising political authority.

49
00:03:36,947 --> 00:03:40,735
You're using force. And force,
my friends, is violence,

50
00:03:40,827 --> 00:03:44,502
the supreme authority from which
all other authority is derived.

51
00:03:44,587 --> 00:03:47,545
Uh, my mother always said
violence never solves anything.

52
00:03:47,627 --> 00:03:49,060
Really?

53
00:03:49,147 --> 00:03:52,457
I wonder what the city fathers
of Hiroshima would say about that.

54
00:03:52,547 --> 00:03:54,299
You.

55
00:03:54,387 --> 00:03:58,096
They probably wouldn't say anything.
Hiroshima was destroyed.

56
00:03:58,187 --> 00:03:59,461
Correct.

57
00:03:59,547 --> 00:04:01,617
Naked force has resolved
more issues...

58
00:04:01,707 --> 00:04:04,141
throughout history
than any other factor.

59
00:04:04,227 --> 00:04:07,537
The contrary opinion, that
violence never solves anything,

60
00:04:07,627 --> 00:04:09,822
is wishful thinking
at its worst.

61
00:04:09,907 --> 00:04:12,944
People who forget that
always pay.

62
00:04:13,027 --> 00:04:16,463
Rico, what's the moral
difference, if any...

63
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:18,424
between a civilian
and a citizen?

64
00:04:18,507 --> 00:04:21,419
A citizen accepts personal
responsibility for the safety...

65
00:04:21,507 --> 00:04:24,658
of the body politic,
defending it with his life.

66
00:04:24,747 --> 00:04:28,660
- A civilian does not.
- The exact words of the text.

67
00:04:28,747 --> 00:04:31,420
But do you understand it?
Do you believe it?

68
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:35,500
- I don't know.
- Of course you don't.

69
00:04:35,587 --> 00:04:37,578
I doubt anyone here would
recognize civic virtue...

70
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:39,385
if it reached up
and bit you in the ass.

71
00:04:56,747 --> 00:04:58,465
Not here.

72
00:04:58,547 --> 00:05:00,583
Come on, let's see if they
posted the math final.

73
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:03,784
- Rico, we gonna take Tesla?
- We're gonna kill 'em.

74
00:05:06,587 --> 00:05:09,226
Remember, all graduating seniors
must fill out a 710 form.

75
00:05:09,307 --> 00:05:11,616
First thing Fleet Academy
looks at is your math scores.

76
00:05:11,707 --> 00:05:13,026
Wish me luck.

77
00:05:20,107 --> 00:05:22,985
- Way to go.
- Good job.

78
00:05:23,067 --> 00:05:25,183
Your turn.
Hold on.

79
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:27,735
I want to talk to Marco.
His sister's at Fleet.

80
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:29,579
- Marco.
- Hi, Carmen.

81
00:05:29,667 --> 00:05:32,056
- What do you hear about Roxy?
- She made pilot.

82
00:05:32,147 --> 00:05:34,980
- She did?
- Oh, yeah.

83
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:37,456
Thirty-five percent.
Very nice.

84
00:05:39,147 --> 00:05:43,618
Look at that. Thirty-five
percent, ladies and gentlemen.

85
00:05:43,707 --> 00:05:44,935
Big numbers.

86
00:05:45,027 --> 00:05:46,824
- Carl.
- Sorry.

87
00:05:53,507 --> 00:05:55,975
So, you haven't done it yet,
have you? Don't lie.

88
00:05:56,067 --> 00:05:57,705
I'm not in any hurry.

89
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,819
- Others are waiting.
- And?

90
00:06:02,227 --> 00:06:03,945
- Did you read her mind?
- Don't have to.

91
00:06:04,027 --> 00:06:06,177
It's pretty clear
what she wants.

92
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:08,576
Yeah, but I want Carmen.

93
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:10,737
- Aw, you got it bad.
- Bye, Marco.

94
00:06:10,827 --> 00:06:12,146
Hey, don't forget about
this afternoon.

95
00:06:12,227 --> 00:06:14,741
He's always late when he walks
you home to fish for a kiss.

96
00:06:14,827 --> 00:06:16,738
Get out of here.

97
00:06:16,827 --> 00:06:19,899
- Marco's sister made pilot.
- So will you.

98
00:06:19,987 --> 00:06:23,946
I mean, imagine flying a half
a million tons of starship.

99
00:06:24,027 --> 00:06:25,585
You gotta have
nerves of steel.

100
00:06:25,667 --> 00:06:28,101
Yeah, you do. Let's see
how yours hold up.

101
00:06:28,187 --> 00:06:29,302
You may begin.

102
00:06:40,107 --> 00:06:42,826
Aw, come on, it's just a bug.
You better put your goggles on.

103
00:06:42,907 --> 00:06:44,306
"Just a bug."

104
00:06:44,387 --> 00:06:48,266
We humans like to think we are
nature's finest achievement.

105
00:06:48,347 --> 00:06:50,497
I'm afraid
it just isn't true.

106
00:06:50,587 --> 00:06:54,865
This Arkellian sand beetle
is superior in many ways.

107
00:06:54,947 --> 00:06:59,463
It reproduces in vast
numbers, has no ego...

108
00:06:59,547 --> 00:07:03,426
has no fear, doesn't
now about death...

109
00:07:03,507 --> 00:07:07,216
and so is the perfect
selfless member of society.

110
00:07:07,307 --> 00:07:09,696
But humans have created
art, mathematics...

111
00:07:09,787 --> 00:07:12,301
and interstellar travel.

112
00:07:12,387 --> 00:07:15,265
True. But before you
let that go to your head...

113
00:07:15,347 --> 00:07:17,577
take the example
of the Arachnids...

114
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:20,784
a highly evolved
insect society.

115
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:23,745
By human standards,
they are relatively stupid...

116
00:07:23,827 --> 00:07:27,706
but their evolution stretches
over millions of years...

117
00:07:28,947 --> 00:07:30,175
- and now...
- Here, take this.

118
00:07:30,267 --> 00:07:32,576
they can
colonize planets...

119
00:07:32,667 --> 00:07:35,465
by hurling their spore
into space.

120
00:07:35,547 --> 00:07:37,697
Okay, I think we got it.

121
00:07:37,787 --> 00:07:39,061
That's the heart.

122
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:42,339
And here's the stomach.

123
00:07:47,947 --> 00:07:49,699
Nerves of steel, huh?

124
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:37,380
Don't think about it.
Just go on instinct.

125
00:09:37,467 --> 00:09:39,219
Try to visualize it.

126
00:09:53,027 --> 00:09:55,382
I see the ace of spades.

127
00:09:59,587 --> 00:10:00,781
You know,
statistically speaking,

128
00:10:00,867 --> 00:10:03,586
you should have accidentally
guessed right by now.

129
00:10:03,667 --> 00:10:08,297
- Try another.
- So my psychic abilities
are zero and I'm unlucky.

130
00:10:08,387 --> 00:10:10,343
No, luck's not a factor.

131
00:10:10,427 --> 00:10:13,180
No one really knows why some people
are sensitive and some aren't.

132
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:16,259
Who knows? Maybe it's a new
stage of human evolution.

133
00:10:16,347 --> 00:10:19,066
That's why they do these
kind of Federal studies.

134
00:10:19,147 --> 00:10:22,059
What-- Cyrano--
Oh, shit. Time out.

135
00:10:22,147 --> 00:10:23,466
Oh, he just wants
some attention.

136
00:10:23,547 --> 00:10:25,105
You don't play
with him any more.

137
00:10:25,187 --> 00:10:26,336
Cyrano.

138
00:10:28,667 --> 00:10:31,340
Go bug Mom, Cyrano.

139
00:10:40,547 --> 00:10:42,503
How do you make him do that?

140
00:10:42,587 --> 00:10:45,863
Oh, I gave him the impression
there's a grub crawling up my mom's leg.

141
00:10:45,947 --> 00:10:47,619
He's on a mission
to go eat it.

142
00:10:47,707 --> 00:10:53,100
Ow! Oh! Get out!
Get off my leg! Oh! Carl!

143
00:10:55,147 --> 00:10:57,138
I sure hope you don't do
anything like that to me.

144
00:10:57,227 --> 00:11:01,982
Don't be afraid.
Can't do human. Yet.

145
00:11:02,067 --> 00:11:03,944
Yeah!

146
00:11:09,267 --> 00:11:10,939
All right!

147
00:11:16,827 --> 00:11:20,456
- Yeah! Yeah!
- Touchdown Tigers.

148
00:11:20,547 --> 00:11:22,856
And the score
is now 4 1-38.

149
00:11:22,947 --> 00:11:24,938
Tigers lead
with 2.:46 remaining...

150
00:11:25,027 --> 00:11:27,097
here at the Buenos Aires
Sports Arena.

151
00:11:27,187 --> 00:11:28,540
Time out Giants.

152
00:11:28,627 --> 00:11:32,097
- Are you all right?
- Much better.

153
00:11:32,187 --> 00:11:33,506
- Now.
- Good.
- Yeah!

154
00:11:33,587 --> 00:11:36,055
All right!
Way to go, team!

155
00:11:36,147 --> 00:11:37,819
Hey! Your helmet.

156
00:11:39,627 --> 00:11:41,345
So, what are you doing
after the game?

157
00:11:43,187 --> 00:11:45,906
Well, everyone's going
to the dance, aren't you?

158
00:11:45,987 --> 00:11:48,455
I don't know. It's my
last night as a civilian.

159
00:11:48,547 --> 00:11:51,015
- Come on, number 12! Let's go!
- Ship out for Tereshkova tomorrow.

160
00:11:51,107 --> 00:11:54,656
- You're going to the Fleet Academy?
- Uh-huh.

161
00:11:54,747 --> 00:11:56,066
That's where
I want to go!

162
00:11:56,147 --> 00:11:58,661
Come on, number 12!
Let's play ball!

163
00:11:58,747 --> 00:12:00,385
Don't get any ideas
about my girlfriend!

164
00:12:04,147 --> 00:12:06,980
All is fair
in love and war.

165
00:12:07,067 --> 00:12:10,139
- Giants! Giants!
-Johnny! Yeah!

166
00:12:10,227 --> 00:12:11,421
Hut! Hut!

167
00:12:23,187 --> 00:12:24,745
Hey, yeah!

168
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:28,422
Giants leading 43-4 1.
Just over 4 2 seconds remaining.

169
00:12:32,107 --> 00:12:33,335
- Yeah!
- All right, let's go.

170
00:12:33,427 --> 00:12:35,258
Irvin, Lathom,
cover the rush.

171
00:12:35,347 --> 00:12:38,225
Perry, fake left.
Bertolli, you go long.

172
00:12:38,307 --> 00:12:42,505
Rico, flip six three hole.
Got it? Hey, Rico?

173
00:12:42,587 --> 00:12:44,862
- Hey!
- What?

174
00:12:44,947 --> 00:12:48,383
You're drifting! Flip six,
three hole, on one! Got it?

175
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:51,618
-Just throw me the ball, Diz.
- Ready? Break!

176
00:12:51,707 --> 00:12:52,935
Break!

177
00:12:54,227 --> 00:12:57,503
Down. Set.
Tight left.

178
00:12:57,587 --> 00:12:59,498
- Screen!
- Hut!

179
00:13:10,907 --> 00:13:13,819
Yeah! Go, go, go!

180
00:13:15,867 --> 00:13:17,744
All right!

181
00:13:20,787 --> 00:13:22,937
Yeah!

182
00:13:23,027 --> 00:13:25,382
He's in there.
It's over.

183
00:13:40,867 --> 00:13:43,062
Who said you could
grow up so fast, huh?

184
00:13:43,147 --> 00:13:45,103
Mom, don't get mushy.

185
00:13:46,987 --> 00:13:48,898
This came for you today.

186
00:13:48,987 --> 00:13:50,784
I presume,
at your request.

187
00:13:54,387 --> 00:13:56,423
A lot of my friends are
doing Federal Service.

188
00:13:56,507 --> 00:13:58,862
Well, you're not
thinking of applying?

189
00:13:58,947 --> 00:14:00,903
Have you lost your mind?

190
00:14:00,987 --> 00:14:04,059
I'd rather take ten lashes in Public
Square than see you ruin your life.

191
00:14:04,147 --> 00:14:06,297
It's a term of service.

192
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:08,218
It's not a career.

193
00:14:08,307 --> 00:14:10,343
I just want to get
out on my own...

194
00:14:11,827 --> 00:14:14,136
see the galaxy
for a couple years.

195
00:14:14,227 --> 00:14:16,536
Johnny, people get killed
in the Federal Service.

196
00:14:16,627 --> 00:14:20,176
Who gave you this idea?
It's that teacher, isn't it?

197
00:14:20,267 --> 00:14:23,065
What's his name? You know
the one I'm talking about.

198
00:14:24,147 --> 00:14:27,105
- Mr Rasczak.
- Rasczak?

199
00:14:29,107 --> 00:14:31,257
Silly name. There should
be a law against...

200
00:14:31,347 --> 00:14:33,417
using a school
as a recruiting station.

201
00:14:33,507 --> 00:14:37,705
No, Rasczak doesn't do that
at all.

202
00:14:37,787 --> 00:14:39,778
He sort of discourages you.

203
00:14:39,867 --> 00:14:41,585
Well, that's good.

204
00:14:41,667 --> 00:14:44,579
'Cause you're going to Harvard,
and that's the end of it.

205
00:14:44,667 --> 00:14:47,056
It's my decision,
not yours.

206
00:14:47,147 --> 00:14:49,661
- Oh, is that how it is, huh?
- Wait, you two.

207
00:14:49,747 --> 00:14:53,057
Uh, Dad and I have a surprise
for you that will settle this.

208
00:14:53,147 --> 00:14:55,502
Can you guess what it is?

209
00:14:55,587 --> 00:14:56,861
No.

210
00:14:57,987 --> 00:14:59,625
You wanted to see the galaxy?

211
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:03,745
How about a trip
to the Outer Rings?

212
00:15:03,827 --> 00:15:06,625
Zegema Beach. Huh?

213
00:15:09,067 --> 00:15:10,580
I've always wanted
to go there.

214
00:15:10,667 --> 00:15:13,101
Good, good.
Then it's all settled.

215
00:15:29,427 --> 00:15:31,657
Sure. Don't go away.

216
00:15:31,747 --> 00:15:33,544
I'm just gonna
go see Mr Rasczak.

217
00:15:35,547 --> 00:15:37,503
Hey, Rico, do you
want to dance?

218
00:15:37,587 --> 00:15:39,100
Actually, Diz,
I promised Carmen--

219
00:15:39,187 --> 00:15:41,064
Aw, come on. Too bad for her
if she's not around.

220
00:15:44,667 --> 00:15:47,306
You know, it's sad.
After tonight, most of us...

221
00:15:47,387 --> 00:15:49,184
probably won't
see each other again.

222
00:15:52,667 --> 00:15:54,623
So, you still
gonna play for Rio?

223
00:15:56,587 --> 00:15:58,942
Yeah, looks like.
Unless Tokyo lets me start.

224
00:15:59,027 --> 00:16:01,177
Well, anyone
who gets you is lucky.

225
00:16:02,507 --> 00:16:05,067
Johnny, how come
we never got together?

226
00:16:08,907 --> 00:16:10,784
Can't we just
be friends, Diz?

227
00:16:13,387 --> 00:16:14,706
Sure.

228
00:16:18,267 --> 00:16:20,098
- Thank you.
- Good night.

229
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:23,736
Look, Diz, I want to talk
to Mr Rasczak.

230
00:16:26,067 --> 00:16:28,376
Well, you better hurry up
if you want to catch him.

231
00:16:28,467 --> 00:16:29,741
You're the best.

232
00:16:42,387 --> 00:16:43,900
Mr Rasczak!

233
00:16:43,987 --> 00:16:46,820
- What is it, Rico?
- I want to thank you.

234
00:16:46,907 --> 00:16:49,375
Your class was the best one
I had this year.

235
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:51,935
Well, it's really not my job to please.
I just hope you learned something.

236
00:16:52,027 --> 00:16:53,699
Well, I want to join up.

237
00:16:53,787 --> 00:16:55,618
I think I got what it takes
to be a citizen.

238
00:16:55,707 --> 00:16:57,982
Good for you.
Go find out.

239
00:16:58,067 --> 00:16:59,898
Well, my parents
are against it.

240
00:16:59,987 --> 00:17:01,500
And I know it's my choice.

241
00:17:01,587 --> 00:17:03,305
I was wondering...

242
00:17:03,387 --> 00:17:04,615
what would you do
if you were me?

243
00:17:05,747 --> 00:17:06,975
Figuring things out
for yourself...

244
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:09,217
is the only freedom
anyone really has.

245
00:17:09,307 --> 00:17:10,660
Use that freedom.

246
00:17:10,747 --> 00:17:12,863
Make up your own mind, Rico.

247
00:17:19,587 --> 00:17:22,055
But I have not been
to paradise

248
00:17:24,147 --> 00:17:27,981
No, I have not been
to paradise

249
00:17:28,987 --> 00:17:31,740
Watch the days go by

250
00:17:31,827 --> 00:17:33,658
All is fine

251
00:17:33,747 --> 00:17:35,260
Don't exaggerate.

252
00:17:35,347 --> 00:17:38,225
I'm serious. I think you have
really beautiful eyes.

253
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,059
- You know?
-Johnny.

254
00:17:42,547 --> 00:17:44,697
Uh, this is Zander.

255
00:17:44,787 --> 00:17:47,426
Yeah, we know each other
from the game.

256
00:17:47,507 --> 00:17:52,217
- No hard feelings?
- No, none at all. We won.

257
00:17:52,307 --> 00:17:55,902
Come on, Carmen.
It's the last dance.

258
00:17:55,987 --> 00:17:57,898
Well, maybe I'll see you
at the Academy.

259
00:17:57,987 --> 00:17:59,261
Yeah. Who knows?

260
00:18:01,427 --> 00:18:05,739
- Good luck.
- Zander's going for pilot too.

261
00:18:07,187 --> 00:18:09,496
You two have
so much in common.

262
00:18:09,587 --> 00:18:12,545
Johnny Rico,
are you jealous?

263
00:18:12,627 --> 00:18:15,187
Well, maybe.

264
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:17,337
You don't have
to be jealous.

265
00:18:21,507 --> 00:18:23,020
Hey, hey,
break it up, you two.

266
00:18:23,107 --> 00:18:25,496
There's a place
for that sort of thing.

267
00:18:28,387 --> 00:18:31,982
I've been thinking,
and I'm gonna do it, Carmen.

268
00:18:32,067 --> 00:18:33,864
I'm gonna go
for Federal Service.

269
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:36,142
That's great.

270
00:18:36,227 --> 00:18:39,025
Carl and I are signing up
tomorrow. Come with us.

271
00:18:39,107 --> 00:18:40,381
I will.

272
00:18:45,987 --> 00:18:49,024
My father's
not home tonight.

273
00:18:49,987 --> 00:18:51,739
All is well

274
00:18:54,707 --> 00:18:58,302
All is well

275
00:18:59,427 --> 00:19:01,657
Talk about it

276
00:19:01,747 --> 00:19:04,136
Watch the days go by

277
00:19:04,227 --> 00:19:06,377
All is well

278
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:08,537
2 4th century dies

279
00:19:08,627 --> 00:19:12,063
I do now,
of my own free will...

280
00:19:12,147 --> 00:19:15,423
after having been
duly advised and warned...

281
00:19:15,507 --> 00:19:18,624
of the meaning and consequences
of this oath...

282
00:19:18,707 --> 00:19:20,857
enrol in the Federal Service...

283
00:19:20,947 --> 00:19:23,097
for not less than two years...

284
00:19:23,187 --> 00:19:26,145
and as much longer
as may be required...

285
00:19:26,227 --> 00:19:28,297
by the needs
of the Federation.

286
00:19:29,387 --> 00:19:31,343
- All set?
- Thank you.

287
00:19:35,387 --> 00:19:38,026
Fresh meat
for the grinder, eh?

288
00:19:39,427 --> 00:19:43,102
- So, how'd you kids do?
- I'm gonna be a pilot.

289
00:19:43,187 --> 00:19:47,066
Well, good for you. We need
all the pilots we can get.

290
00:19:48,707 --> 00:19:51,460
- Hey, did you get starside R and D?
- No.

291
00:19:51,547 --> 00:19:54,903
- I don't believe it.
- I got Games and Theory.

292
00:19:54,987 --> 00:19:56,943
Games and Theory?

293
00:19:57,027 --> 00:19:59,461
- That's military intelligence.
- Yeah.

294
00:19:59,547 --> 00:20:01,742
Way to go, Carl.

295
00:20:01,827 --> 00:20:04,421
Next time we meet,
I'll probably have to salute you.

296
00:20:04,507 --> 00:20:05,906
Hmm.

297
00:20:07,227 --> 00:20:09,058
How about you, son?

298
00:20:09,147 --> 00:20:11,945
- Infantry, sir.
- Good for you.

299
00:20:12,027 --> 00:20:14,495
Mobile Infantry made me
the man I am today.

300
00:20:16,107 --> 00:20:19,622
All recruits must report to the
Federal Transportation Hub...

301
00:20:19,707 --> 00:20:21,265
within 2 4 hours.

302
00:20:21,347 --> 00:20:23,861
Welcome to the adventure
of Federal Service.

303
00:20:23,947 --> 00:20:26,142
Let's make a vow.

304
00:20:26,227 --> 00:20:29,537
No matter what,
we'll always be friends.

305
00:20:31,187 --> 00:20:32,302
I'll go for that.

306
00:20:33,947 --> 00:20:36,177
Well, chances are we'll
never see each other again.

307
00:20:37,867 --> 00:20:40,825
We'll be millions of light-years
away from each other.

308
00:20:40,907 --> 00:20:43,296
But, uh, yeah, sure.
Why not?

309
00:20:45,747 --> 00:20:47,578
You'll resign, and that's
all there is to it.

310
00:20:47,667 --> 00:20:50,420
It may look bad, but if that's
the worst you suffer, then that's fine.

311
00:20:50,507 --> 00:20:53,305
- I won't quit!
- I'm telling you, you will.

312
00:20:53,387 --> 00:20:55,378
You're not going back.
You're going on vacation!

313
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:57,298
I am not going
on vacation!

314
00:20:57,387 --> 00:20:59,105
I want to be a citizen.

315
00:20:59,187 --> 00:21:00,586
It's my decision.
I made it.

316
00:21:00,667 --> 00:21:02,498
You walk out that door,
you are cut off, young man.

317
00:21:02,587 --> 00:21:04,100
You understand me?

318
00:21:04,187 --> 00:21:06,496
All right, that's it!
You are cut off!

319
00:21:06,587 --> 00:21:08,418
Johnny, why won't you
change your mind?

320
00:21:08,507 --> 00:21:10,543
Does citizenship
mean that much to you?

321
00:21:11,387 --> 00:21:13,423
Well, yeah, sure.

322
00:21:13,507 --> 00:21:15,338
Well, I hope so.

323
00:21:15,427 --> 00:21:17,861
I hope you don't ruin your life
over some silly little girl...

324
00:21:17,947 --> 00:21:19,824
who wants to look handsome
in a uniform.

325
00:21:19,907 --> 00:21:22,137
- Don't talk about Carmen that way!
-Johnny.

326
00:21:22,227 --> 00:21:24,024
Your attention, please.

327
00:21:24,107 --> 00:21:28,259
Outbound group 1380,
all hub 29 connections.

328
00:21:28,347 --> 00:21:29,939
- Do you have everything?
- Moscow now boarding...

329
00:21:30,027 --> 00:21:31,824
- Great.
- at bank 8-A.

330
00:21:37,147 --> 00:21:40,378
-Johnny.
- Be a good girl, hear?

331
00:21:40,467 --> 00:21:43,061
- You're late.
- My dad had to help me pack.

332
00:21:43,147 --> 00:21:45,786
Suddenly he's afraid he's never
gonna see me again or something.

333
00:21:45,867 --> 00:21:48,256
It was sweet,
but it took forever.

334
00:21:48,347 --> 00:21:52,898
Oh. Anyway, I guess
I'm ready to go.

335
00:21:52,987 --> 00:21:55,865
Yeah, me too. I'm wearing
everything I own.

336
00:21:58,587 --> 00:22:00,418
I'm sorry your parents
were mad.

337
00:22:00,507 --> 00:22:02,782
Who cares? The Federation
will give me...

338
00:22:02,867 --> 00:22:05,062
everything I need for
the next two years, right?

339
00:22:06,627 --> 00:22:10,176
- You talk to Carl?
- Yeah, he left this morning.

340
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:13,942
- Couldn't say where.
- Oh, it's exciting, going away.

341
00:22:14,027 --> 00:22:16,700
But I'm scared.
Aren't you?

342
00:22:21,467 --> 00:22:23,298
I'm gonna miss you.

343
00:22:24,667 --> 00:22:26,817
I'm gonna miss you too.

344
00:22:27,707 --> 00:22:29,698
I love you.

345
00:22:29,787 --> 00:22:32,745
Outbound group 94B
to Tereshkova--

346
00:22:32,827 --> 00:22:34,499
That's me.

347
00:22:36,787 --> 00:22:40,575
Just say it once.
Try it on for size.

348
00:22:44,107 --> 00:22:45,426
I love you.

349
00:22:53,667 --> 00:22:55,703
Don't forget to write.

350
00:22:55,787 --> 00:22:57,106
I won't.

351
00:23:11,787 --> 00:23:14,255
Fully automatic Morita.
Who wants to hold it?

352
00:23:14,347 --> 00:23:15,541
Me! Me! Me! Me! Me!

353
00:23:15,627 --> 00:23:19,745
Citizen rule. People
making a better tomorrow.

354
00:23:27,707 --> 00:23:30,619
A murderer was captured
this morning and tried today.

355
00:23:30,707 --> 00:23:32,538
Guilty.

356
00:23:33,827 --> 00:23:35,419
Sentence.: death.

357
00:23:35,507 --> 00:23:38,579
Execution tonight at 6.:00.
All net. All channels.

358
00:23:46,387 --> 00:23:49,185
If you think you're psychic,

359
00:23:49,267 --> 00:23:50,416
maybe you are.

360
00:23:52,627 --> 00:23:55,539
Federal studies are being
conducted in your community.

361
00:23:58,787 --> 00:24:02,621
Every school kid knows
that Arachnids are dangerous.

362
00:24:07,987 --> 00:24:10,865
However, Mormon extremists
disregarded Federal warnings...

363
00:24:10,947 --> 00:24:15,020
and established Fort Joe Smith deep
inside the Arachnid Quarantine Zone.

364
00:24:15,107 --> 00:24:19,100
Too late, they realized that Dantana had
already been chosen by other colonists.:

365
00:24:19,187 --> 00:24:21,018
Arachnids.

366
00:24:26,227 --> 00:24:28,695
- One, two, three, four!
- Ten-hut!

367
00:24:28,787 --> 00:24:31,665
- One, two, three, four!
- Most of you will not...

368
00:24:31,747 --> 00:24:34,341
live to be
in the Mobile Infantry.

369
00:24:34,427 --> 00:24:36,987
The trouble is, you are not
good enough the way you are.

370
00:24:37,067 --> 00:24:39,103
Hands at your side!

371
00:24:39,187 --> 00:24:40,506
Chin up.

372
00:24:40,587 --> 00:24:43,260
I am your senior drill instructor,
Career Sergeant Zim!

373
00:24:43,347 --> 00:24:46,066
Suck in that gut!
Feet together!

374
00:24:48,787 --> 00:24:51,017
To think this had
to happen to me.

375
00:24:51,107 --> 00:24:53,416
What a bunch of apes.
No, strike that!

376
00:24:53,507 --> 00:24:54,735
You don't rate that good.

377
00:24:54,827 --> 00:24:56,783
Never in my life
have I seen--

378
00:24:59,427 --> 00:25:01,543
Do you think I'm funny?
Do I make you laugh?

379
00:25:01,627 --> 00:25:04,187
- Do you think I'm a comedian, son?
- I'm sorry.

380
00:25:04,267 --> 00:25:08,226
The first words and the last words out
of your stinking holes will be "Sir"!

381
00:25:08,307 --> 00:25:10,343
- Do you get me?
- Sir, yes, sir!

382
00:25:10,427 --> 00:25:12,782
You see that armoury?
Run around it.

383
00:25:12,867 --> 00:25:15,097
Run, I said!
Run, run, run!

384
00:25:15,187 --> 00:25:17,098
- Bronski, keep pace!
- Move! Move!

385
00:25:17,187 --> 00:25:19,576
Now, anytime you think
I'm being too tough...

386
00:25:19,667 --> 00:25:21,464
anytime you think
I'm being unfair...

387
00:25:21,547 --> 00:25:24,903
anytime you miss
your mommy, quit!

388
00:25:24,987 --> 00:25:27,296
You sign form 1240-A,
you grab your gear...

389
00:25:27,387 --> 00:25:29,821
you take a stroll
down Washout Lane!

390
00:25:29,907 --> 00:25:31,579
Do you get me?

391
00:25:31,667 --> 00:25:33,817
- Sir, yes, sir!
- Pathetic!

392
00:25:33,907 --> 00:25:37,980
I wonder if there's a handful of
guts in the whole bunch of you.

393
00:25:38,067 --> 00:25:42,902
Now, who here thinks they got
what it takes to knock me down?

394
00:25:42,987 --> 00:25:45,660
Sir! I guess
maybe I do, sir!

395
00:25:55,027 --> 00:25:58,258
Ow! God! God!

396
00:26:00,267 --> 00:26:02,383
- You all right, son?
- Sir, yes, sir!

397
00:26:02,467 --> 00:26:05,618
It's my arm.
I think it's broken, sir.

398
00:26:05,707 --> 00:26:08,460
- Medic!
- God.

399
00:26:08,547 --> 00:26:11,345
Pain is in your mind!

400
00:26:11,427 --> 00:26:13,258
- Who's next?
- Sir!

401
00:26:13,347 --> 00:26:16,066
Recruit Flores reporting
for duty, sir!

402
00:26:25,107 --> 00:26:28,543
You specifically requested transfer from
Fort Cronkite to this training unit?

403
00:26:28,627 --> 00:26:30,265
Sir, I heard
it was the best, sir!

404
00:26:30,347 --> 00:26:33,339
It is the best.

405
00:26:33,427 --> 00:26:36,225
But what makes you think
you're good enough?

406
00:26:42,867 --> 00:26:44,823
Now that's the kind of gal
who makes squad leader.

407
00:26:44,907 --> 00:26:47,057
That's my job
you're talking about.

408
00:26:48,747 --> 00:26:49,975
Come on.

409
00:26:50,067 --> 00:26:51,261
- Here we go!
- Here we go!

410
00:26:51,347 --> 00:26:52,541
- Roughnecks!
- Roughnecks!

411
00:26:52,627 --> 00:26:53,901
- On the go!
- On the go!

412
00:27:03,827 --> 00:27:06,785
One, two, three, four...

413
00:27:06,867 --> 00:27:09,984
one, two, MI!

414
00:27:13,107 --> 00:27:14,825
You know, I'd like
to kill that Sergeant Zim.

415
00:27:14,907 --> 00:27:17,296
- Whoa, improper attitude!
- Watch it.

416
00:27:17,387 --> 00:27:19,423
- They'll kick you out
for talking like that.
- Bye-bye.

417
00:27:19,507 --> 00:27:21,498
There you go
down Washout Lane.

418
00:27:21,587 --> 00:27:23,896
Yup, you either got what
it takes, or you don't.

419
00:27:23,987 --> 00:27:26,103
- Hey, there is a line.
- Wait your turn, Ace.

420
00:27:26,187 --> 00:27:29,702
Hey, at ease, little soldier.
It's all the same muck.

421
00:27:29,787 --> 00:27:31,300
Get in line
like everyone else.

422
00:27:41,027 --> 00:27:43,780
You got some guts
for a rich kid.

423
00:27:43,867 --> 00:27:46,256
I guess you and me could be
buddies. What do you say?

424
00:27:46,347 --> 00:27:47,746
Oh-oh, that is
no way to act.

425
00:27:47,827 --> 00:27:50,864
- I'm honoured.
- Hey! Of course you are.

426
00:27:50,947 --> 00:27:52,983
Everybody should have
a friend like me.

427
00:27:53,067 --> 00:27:55,217
Come on, Ace. Back of the line
now! Back of the line!

428
00:27:55,307 --> 00:27:56,535
- Back, back, back, back!
- All right. Hurry up, hurry up.

429
00:27:56,627 --> 00:27:58,140
- What a jerk, man.
- Tough guy.

430
00:28:00,187 --> 00:28:02,064
Hey, Rico, want
to sit together?

431
00:28:02,147 --> 00:28:03,466
No thanks, Diz.

432
00:28:05,707 --> 00:28:07,538
What's your malfunction, Rico?

433
00:28:08,907 --> 00:28:10,784
You are.

434
00:28:10,867 --> 00:28:13,506
I joined up to get out on my own,
and you had to tag along.

435
00:28:15,627 --> 00:28:17,822
You think I joined the Mobile
Infantry because of you?

436
00:28:17,907 --> 00:28:19,738
You saying you didn't?

437
00:28:25,907 --> 00:28:27,101
Hi.

438
00:28:27,187 --> 00:28:29,655
Forget about it, Ace.
You don't stand a chance.

439
00:28:29,747 --> 00:28:32,500
What makes you even think you're
gonna make squad leader, Rico?

440
00:28:32,587 --> 00:28:34,179
- Something I got, you don't.
- Ha!

441
00:28:34,267 --> 00:28:36,940
-You rich kids are all the same.
-It isn't about that.

442
00:28:37,027 --> 00:28:39,063
- It's about who's the best.
- Hey!

443
00:28:49,947 --> 00:28:51,380
Third squad!

444
00:28:51,467 --> 00:28:53,822
If someone's hurt, put him on your back
and take him out of there!

445
00:28:53,907 --> 00:28:55,022
Let's go!

446
00:28:56,147 --> 00:28:57,819
Go, Simmons!
Go, go, you sissy!

447
00:28:57,907 --> 00:29:00,740
Sir, I don't understand.

448
00:29:00,827 --> 00:29:02,977
Who needs a knife
in a nuke fight, anyway?

449
00:29:03,067 --> 00:29:06,582
All you gotta do
is push a button, sir.

450
00:29:06,667 --> 00:29:10,899
Cease fire. Put your hand
on that wall, trooper.

451
00:29:14,187 --> 00:29:16,257
Put your hand on that wall!

452
00:29:25,627 --> 00:29:26,946
Damn it.

453
00:29:31,707 --> 00:29:35,746
The enemy cannot push a button
if you disable his hand.

454
00:29:39,387 --> 00:29:40,536
Medic!

455
00:29:41,587 --> 00:29:43,179
Hand me that towel, will you?

456
00:29:43,267 --> 00:29:45,656
Ah, well, we all have
one thing in common.

457
00:29:45,747 --> 00:29:48,545
We were all stupid enough
to sign up for Mobile Infantry.

458
00:29:48,627 --> 00:29:51,585
- Breckinridge, what's your excuse?
- Oh, my family's all farmers.

459
00:29:51,667 --> 00:29:53,498
I hate farming. I mean,
uh, Mobile Infantry--

460
00:29:53,587 --> 00:29:55,418
It's like pure picnic
by comparison.

461
00:29:55,507 --> 00:29:58,783
All right, so they grow 'em big and dumb
on the farm planet, huh?

462
00:29:58,867 --> 00:30:01,142
- And pretty!
- I like big!

463
00:30:01,227 --> 00:30:04,060
- Djana'D, what about you?
- Oh, I'm going in for politics...

464
00:30:04,147 --> 00:30:06,138
and, you know, you gotta be
a citizen for that.

465
00:30:06,227 --> 00:30:09,185
- So here I am.
- Ah, you want some responsibility.

466
00:30:09,267 --> 00:30:12,384
- Yeah.
- Shujimi, come on, let's keep it goin'.

467
00:30:12,467 --> 00:30:14,776
I got into Harvard,
but my father says forget it.

468
00:30:14,867 --> 00:30:16,061
It's gonna cost an arm
and a leg, you know?

469
00:30:16,147 --> 00:30:17,785
So, if I serve,

470
00:30:17,867 --> 00:30:20,381
Federation pays my way.

471
00:30:20,467 --> 00:30:21,820
I want to have babies.

472
00:30:21,907 --> 00:30:24,102
You know, it's a lot easier to
get a licence if you've served.

473
00:30:24,187 --> 00:30:25,825
- So--
- I'm going career.

474
00:30:25,907 --> 00:30:28,501
- Officer's training. All the way.
- Ah!

475
00:30:28,587 --> 00:30:30,782
Future Sky Marshal.
All right, Rico, your turn.

476
00:30:33,267 --> 00:30:34,620
Who asked you to be so nosy?

477
00:30:34,707 --> 00:30:36,698
What? I'm the-the bad guy?
I'm gonna be a writer, you know?

478
00:30:36,787 --> 00:30:39,426
A writer's got
a right to be nosy.

479
00:30:39,507 --> 00:30:42,180
Hey, Flores, you know
Rico from Buenos Aires.

480
00:30:42,267 --> 00:30:46,306
- What's his story?
- Oh, uh,

481
00:30:46,387 --> 00:30:48,298
he's here
because of a girl.

482
00:30:49,107 --> 00:30:52,497
Oh, Rico! Lover boy!

483
00:30:53,907 --> 00:30:56,705
- He's getting me excited.
- He's gonna blow.

484
00:31:00,107 --> 00:31:01,222
Is it you?

485
00:31:05,107 --> 00:31:09,658
This is where we live.
It's not much, but it's home.

486
00:31:09,747 --> 00:31:13,262
Right there, that's my bunk,
where I dream about you every night.

487
00:31:14,707 --> 00:31:16,220
Boot's pretty tough.

488
00:31:16,307 --> 00:31:18,821
Sometimes I think I won't make it.

489
00:31:18,907 --> 00:31:21,102
But then I think about what
you're doing, and I try harder.

490
00:31:22,947 --> 00:31:27,099
- Hey, guys! Do you mind?
- Try harder, baby, try harder!

491
00:31:31,387 --> 00:31:35,266
Who knows? They might even
make me squad leader.

492
00:31:35,347 --> 00:31:37,019
Uh-oh,
I better pack it in.

493
00:31:37,107 --> 00:31:40,543
Oh, I love you, baby,
I love you!

494
00:31:40,627 --> 00:31:44,142
- Write me!
- I love you so much

495
00:31:44,227 --> 00:31:46,821
- I'm gonna kill you guys!
- I love you so much

496
00:31:49,547 --> 00:31:50,741
- Bye! Write me.
- Bye!

497
00:31:52,547 --> 00:31:54,538
Orbit in five, Ibanez.

498
00:31:54,627 --> 00:31:56,379
First one there
gets to fly.

499
00:32:11,427 --> 00:32:13,497
- Locking it down.
- Wait! Wait!

500
00:32:15,467 --> 00:32:18,140
Oh, no. Not Ibanez again.
She's crazy!

501
00:32:18,227 --> 00:32:20,183
Ready, go!

502
00:32:26,507 --> 00:32:27,781
Yeah!

503
00:32:29,547 --> 00:32:30,980
Deploying wings.

504
00:33:13,267 --> 00:33:15,576
How come you're
in such a good mood, huh?

505
00:33:15,667 --> 00:33:17,419
'Cause today
I get to fly that.

506
00:33:39,907 --> 00:33:42,216
Pilot Trainee Ibanez
reporting for duty, ma'am.

507
00:33:42,307 --> 00:33:44,059
Take the number two chair,
Ibanez.

508
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:46,297
- Yes, ma'am.
- You see that?

509
00:33:49,507 --> 00:33:54,501
- Identify.
- Ibanez, T-3 25-A, clear.

510
00:33:59,347 --> 00:34:02,305
What are you doing here?

511
00:34:02,387 --> 00:34:05,140
I'm the guy whose gonna
teach you to fly this crate.

512
00:34:05,227 --> 00:34:07,900
Oh, Assistant Instructor.

513
00:34:08,947 --> 00:34:11,336
Should I call you "sir"?

514
00:34:11,427 --> 00:34:14,260
- Only when I give you an order.
- Prepare for departure.

515
00:34:15,707 --> 00:34:19,143
It's amazing, us running
into each other like this.

516
00:34:19,227 --> 00:34:21,866
- Maybe it's fate.
- Maybe not.

517
00:34:21,947 --> 00:34:24,984
Heard about this crazy girl
coming through the Academy.

518
00:34:25,067 --> 00:34:29,504
Solid math, a little wild
on the stick, but a natural.

519
00:34:29,587 --> 00:34:30,986
And when it turned out
to be you,

520
00:34:31,067 --> 00:34:33,183
I just made sure that we
would run into each other.

521
00:34:33,267 --> 00:34:35,861
Rodger Young cleared for
undocking and departure.

522
00:34:35,947 --> 00:34:37,699
All right, Ibanez.

523
00:34:37,787 --> 00:34:40,017
- Take her out.
- Yes, ma'am.

524
00:34:41,267 --> 00:34:43,098
All systems go.

525
00:35:06,067 --> 00:35:09,503
In simulation, my supervisors
could never keep up.

526
00:35:09,587 --> 00:35:11,305
Well, this isn't simulation any more...

527
00:35:11,387 --> 00:35:13,901
so take her out easy, cadet.

528
00:35:13,987 --> 00:35:15,215
Yes, sir.

529
00:35:23,907 --> 00:35:25,386
Five metres from object.

530
00:35:28,427 --> 00:35:29,906
Three metres from object.

531
00:35:34,467 --> 00:35:35,741
Clear.

532
00:35:38,627 --> 00:35:41,460
- Don't exceed port speed.
- Or what?

533
00:35:41,547 --> 00:35:46,063
Or they revoke your flight
status, and mine.

534
00:35:47,747 --> 00:35:50,022
Your career is
in my hands.

535
00:35:56,907 --> 00:35:58,226
Steady as she goes,
Number Two.

536
00:35:58,307 --> 00:36:00,457
- Prepare for warp.
- Yes, ma'am.

537
00:36:00,547 --> 00:36:03,664
Number One, design
for Jupiter orbit.

538
00:36:03,747 --> 00:36:07,422
All crew, all sections,
stand by to cut in C-drive.

539
00:36:07,507 --> 00:36:11,102
- Star drive in five, four,
- Five, four...

540
00:36:11,187 --> 00:36:13,382
- ready...
- three, two...
- steady...

541
00:36:13,467 --> 00:36:14,946
- one--
- go!

542
00:36:37,987 --> 00:36:39,739
We're going in!
Move!

543
00:36:48,427 --> 00:36:49,780
Man, they're defended.
No way in.

544
00:36:52,147 --> 00:36:54,422
- Flip six, three hole.
- What?

545
00:36:54,507 --> 00:36:57,146
You run a flip six, three
hole play, and you can score.

546
00:36:57,227 --> 00:36:58,546
- Cover me.
- You got it.

547
00:37:06,667 --> 00:37:08,225
Now!

548
00:37:14,547 --> 00:37:16,936
- Thanks, buddy.
- Bastard!

549
00:37:25,707 --> 00:37:27,026
Yeah!

550
00:37:32,427 --> 00:37:34,383
Kid's got some moves.

551
00:37:34,467 --> 00:37:36,264
Give him a squad.
See what he can do.

552
00:37:41,067 --> 00:37:42,785
Kitty, Kitty.

553
00:37:42,867 --> 00:37:45,256
Someone's got to teach you guys
how to play some pool here.

554
00:37:46,467 --> 00:37:47,820
Look at him.

555
00:37:47,907 --> 00:37:50,546
Have you ever seen anybody
so pleased with himself?

556
00:37:50,627 --> 00:37:54,142
Well, Zim must have had to choose
someone to be his brownnose.

557
00:37:55,267 --> 00:37:56,461
All right, where were we?

558
00:37:56,547 --> 00:37:58,378
Okay, watch and learn.
Watch and learn.

559
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:01,779
I couldn't have done it
without you, Diz.

560
00:38:03,587 --> 00:38:04,861
Friends?

561
00:38:07,547 --> 00:38:08,946
Friends.

562
00:38:10,147 --> 00:38:12,615
- Mail call! Levy!
- Yeah, that's me.

563
00:38:12,707 --> 00:38:15,175
- Shujimi!
- Here.

564
00:38:15,267 --> 00:38:16,620
- Rico.
- Here.

565
00:38:16,707 --> 00:38:18,663
- Breckinridge!
- Yeah, right here.

566
00:38:18,747 --> 00:38:21,739
- Niler.
- Yeah, here I am. Ah, great, my dad.

567
00:38:21,827 --> 00:38:23,704
That's all, folks.

568
00:38:30,907 --> 00:38:32,306
Hi, Johnny.

569
00:38:32,387 --> 00:38:34,855
I'm sorry I haven't
written you sooner, but, uh...

570
00:38:34,947 --> 00:38:37,415
- Oh, Rico,
- it's been really busy.
- you don't deserve that!

571
00:38:37,507 --> 00:38:39,384
- Shh, shh.
- They've really got us
going here.

572
00:38:39,467 --> 00:38:41,901
They must have made you
squad leader by now.

573
00:38:41,987 --> 00:38:44,296
And if they haven't,
tell 'em to talk to me.

574
00:38:44,387 --> 00:38:46,537
See? All it takes is
the love of a good woman.

575
00:38:46,627 --> 00:38:48,936
- Yeah.
- That is a woman.
- Beautiful.

576
00:38:49,027 --> 00:38:51,666
- Look at that.
- Look at those.
- Stop it.

577
00:38:51,747 --> 00:38:53,578
- Isn't it beautiful?
- I'm dying.

578
00:38:53,667 --> 00:38:55,703
I love it out here.

579
00:38:57,827 --> 00:39:00,341
- That's also the problem.
- Shh, shh, shh, shh.

580
00:39:00,427 --> 00:39:04,466
Because I think
I'm gonna go career.

581
00:39:05,747 --> 00:39:08,022
I want to command
a ship of my own.

582
00:39:08,107 --> 00:39:09,904
And you know...

583
00:39:11,587 --> 00:39:12,940
I don't think that's gonna
leave a lot of room...

584
00:39:13,027 --> 00:39:15,018
for you and me, Johnny.

585
00:39:16,227 --> 00:39:18,263
- Oh, God.
-Jeez.

586
00:39:18,347 --> 00:39:21,737
I know that's not
what you wanted to hear.

587
00:39:21,827 --> 00:39:23,021
But, uh...

588
00:39:25,187 --> 00:39:29,339
I have to follow my heart.
I'm sorry.

589
00:39:31,307 --> 00:39:34,219
Write me, all right?

590
00:39:34,307 --> 00:39:36,775
Write me so that I know
we'll always be friends.

591
00:39:51,347 --> 00:39:54,384
- Let's get back to the game.
- I feel so sorry for Johnny.

592
00:39:54,467 --> 00:39:55,741
Funny how they always
want to be friends...

593
00:39:55,827 --> 00:39:58,546
after they rip your guts
out, huh?

594
00:39:58,627 --> 00:40:01,300
Yeah. Well,
it's what I deserve.

595
00:40:02,747 --> 00:40:04,578
What are you
talking about?

596
00:40:06,347 --> 00:40:08,144
Oh, I joined up for her.

597
00:40:09,467 --> 00:40:11,617
I wouldn't even be here
if it wasn't for her.

598
00:40:11,707 --> 00:40:14,380
What are you talking about? You
made squad leader on your own.

599
00:40:17,067 --> 00:40:19,535
And, hey, you still got me
to kick around.

600
00:40:24,067 --> 00:40:25,420
Fun and games are over,
children.

601
00:40:25,507 --> 00:40:27,463
You will be firing
live ammunition...

602
00:40:27,547 --> 00:40:29,697
in a simulated combat
environment.

603
00:40:29,787 --> 00:40:33,985
You will exercise extreme
caution on my assault course!

604
00:40:34,067 --> 00:40:36,706
- Do you get me?
- Sir, yes, sir!

605
00:40:36,787 --> 00:40:38,539
Rico, take 'em out!

606
00:40:39,947 --> 00:40:42,984
First fire team with me.
Next team in ten seconds.

607
00:40:43,067 --> 00:40:45,786
Maximum score has been 2 80.

608
00:40:45,867 --> 00:40:49,621
- I expect you to do better!
- Go!

609
00:40:57,507 --> 00:40:59,179
Shujimi, stay down!

610
00:41:07,867 --> 00:41:11,098
Hey! Goddam it, Breckinridge,
clear my line of fire!

611
00:41:11,187 --> 00:41:13,064
It's my helmet!
It's all screwed up!

612
00:41:13,147 --> 00:41:14,819
You're gonna
blow the score!

613
00:41:14,907 --> 00:41:16,386
- Damn!
- Dumb shit!

614
00:41:16,467 --> 00:41:17,820
Diz, stay put!
What's the problem?

615
00:41:17,907 --> 00:41:19,625
- Damn thing keeps getting in my way!
- Give it to me.

616
00:41:19,707 --> 00:41:21,902
How come whenever something goes wrong,
it's always you, Breckinridge?

617
00:41:21,987 --> 00:41:23,340
It must be 'cause
I'm big and dumb!

618
00:41:23,427 --> 00:41:24,985
Yeah, right!

619
00:41:30,787 --> 00:41:32,584
Medic!

620
00:41:35,267 --> 00:41:38,737
Rico, you are relieved
of squad command!

621
00:41:40,707 --> 00:41:43,585
Rico, did you give the recruit
permission to remove his helmet?

622
00:41:43,667 --> 00:41:46,420
Sir, yes, sir. Breckinridge
reported a helmet malfunction...

623
00:41:46,507 --> 00:41:48,065
and I asked him
to show it to me, sir.

624
00:41:48,147 --> 00:41:51,742
Are you rated to repair
the M-3 Tactical Helmet, Rico?

625
00:41:53,387 --> 00:41:54,786
Sir, no, sir!

626
00:41:54,867 --> 00:41:56,698
Then why did you order your man
to remove his helmet...

627
00:41:56,787 --> 00:41:59,255
during a live fire
exercise?

628
00:41:59,347 --> 00:42:02,419
Sir, I needed everyone in
my squad operational, sir!

629
00:42:03,827 --> 00:42:06,182
I wanted to win, sir!

630
00:42:11,867 --> 00:42:13,186
Carry on.

631
00:42:20,307 --> 00:42:24,744
Sergeant, we've already lost
two recruits over this incident.

632
00:42:24,827 --> 00:42:27,785
Do you think there's any possibility
of salvaging this man?

633
00:42:29,547 --> 00:42:30,821
Yes, sir, I do.

634
00:42:32,107 --> 00:42:33,381
All right.

635
00:42:34,867 --> 00:42:36,619
We'll try administrative punishment.

636
00:42:42,227 --> 00:42:44,024
Prisoner, halt!

637
00:43:01,147 --> 00:43:02,978
Bite down on this, son.

638
00:43:03,067 --> 00:43:05,501
It helps.
I know.

639
00:43:15,427 --> 00:43:18,339
For incompetence of command...

640
00:43:18,427 --> 00:43:20,941
for failure to abide
by safety regulations...

641
00:43:21,027 --> 00:43:24,303
during a live fire exercise...

642
00:43:24,387 --> 00:43:27,902
for negligence which contributed
to the death of a teammate...

643
00:43:27,987 --> 00:43:30,137
recruit trainee
John Rico...

644
00:43:30,227 --> 00:43:32,218
is sentenced to
administrative punishment.

645
00:43:33,827 --> 00:43:34,942
Ten lashes.

646
00:43:36,867 --> 00:43:38,698
You may carry out
the sentence.

647
00:43:45,707 --> 00:43:47,663
One!

648
00:43:49,147 --> 00:43:51,103
Two!

649
00:43:52,827 --> 00:43:54,146
Three!

650
00:43:56,067 --> 00:43:57,898
Four!

651
00:43:59,827 --> 00:44:01,385
Five!

652
00:44:03,827 --> 00:44:04,896
Six!

653
00:44:06,707 --> 00:44:07,856
Seven!

654
00:44:09,587 --> 00:44:12,055
Eight!

655
00:44:12,147 --> 00:44:13,421
Nine!

656
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:16,346
Ten!

657
00:44:28,187 --> 00:44:31,099
All sections secure.
EBS is high normal.

658
00:44:31,187 --> 00:44:33,985
Switching to slave on my mark.
Mark.

659
00:44:37,747 --> 00:44:39,544
Thanks.
You read my mind.

660
00:44:41,307 --> 00:44:44,299
Oh, third watch always
seems to last forever.

661
00:44:44,387 --> 00:44:45,979
I don't know.

662
00:44:46,067 --> 00:44:48,422
It depends on who
you're spending it with.

663
00:44:51,107 --> 00:44:52,859
Something's wrong.

664
00:44:57,147 --> 00:45:00,981
- There.
- No, I replotted the course.

665
00:45:01,067 --> 00:45:04,104
- It's more efficient this way.
- Three weeks aboard a starship...

666
00:45:04,187 --> 00:45:06,337
and you think that you
can lick my navs?

667
00:45:06,427 --> 00:45:07,621
Check it.

668
00:45:12,587 --> 00:45:15,545
You know, I was talking
with Captain Deladier...

669
00:45:15,627 --> 00:45:17,026
and, uh, she said--

670
00:45:17,107 --> 00:45:19,575
Don't change the subject.

671
00:45:19,667 --> 00:45:20,861
Am I right?

672
00:45:27,987 --> 00:45:30,865
Yeah. Yeah.
You're right.

673
00:45:30,947 --> 00:45:33,177
So, what did
the captain say?

674
00:45:34,547 --> 00:45:37,186
She thinks that we ought
to team up officially...

675
00:45:39,147 --> 00:45:41,820
and crew for her.

676
00:45:41,907 --> 00:45:45,263
- You and me, huh?
- We're good together, Carmen.

677
00:45:45,347 --> 00:45:48,544
We're way ahead of the curve
in every department.

678
00:45:48,627 --> 00:45:51,505
I can anticipate you.

679
00:45:51,587 --> 00:45:54,226
You know what I want.

680
00:45:55,827 --> 00:45:58,944
No. What do you want?

681
00:46:06,467 --> 00:46:08,219
There's a gravity field
out there.

682
00:46:10,427 --> 00:46:12,622
- Run a scan. Sensors on.
- There.

683
00:46:15,187 --> 00:46:18,304
- Gravity at 225 and rising.
- Report.

684
00:46:18,387 --> 00:46:20,264
Captain, we're in the path
of an unidentified object...

685
00:46:20,347 --> 00:46:21,985
moving toward us
at high speed.

686
00:46:22,067 --> 00:46:24,262
Profile suggests
an asteroid, ma'am.

687
00:46:36,027 --> 00:46:38,621
- Impact, six seconds!
- Emergency evasion!

688
00:46:43,427 --> 00:46:45,816
Three, two,

689
00:46:48,787 --> 00:46:50,015
fire!

690
00:47:04,307 --> 00:47:05,979
Close compartment 21!

691
00:47:19,547 --> 00:47:20,900
Where'd it come from?

692
00:47:20,987 --> 00:47:23,706
It came out of the Arachnid
Quarantine Zone, ma'am.

693
00:47:25,587 --> 00:47:28,385
Number Four, contact Fleet.
Tell 'em there's a loose asteroid
headed their way.

694
00:47:28,467 --> 00:47:30,503
Communications are down,
ma'am. They're gone.

695
00:47:32,147 --> 00:47:34,945
- Damage assessment.
- Hull's compromised.

696
00:47:35,027 --> 00:47:36,460
We're lucky
to be alive, ma'am.

697
00:47:36,547 --> 00:47:38,344
Luck didn't have anything
to do with it.

698
00:47:39,627 --> 00:47:41,379
We have a hell
of a flight team.

699
00:47:56,147 --> 00:47:58,422
It really stinks, you going.

700
00:47:58,507 --> 00:48:01,226
Yeah, well, the Mobile Infantry
will just have to get along without me.

701
00:48:05,267 --> 00:48:07,986
I don't get it, Rico.
You took your licks.

702
00:48:08,067 --> 00:48:09,659
If they didn't want you,
they would have kicked you out.

703
00:48:09,747 --> 00:48:11,066
Hey--

704
00:48:12,507 --> 00:48:14,463
I joined up for the wrong reasons.
I got a guy killed.

705
00:48:14,547 --> 00:48:16,777
I figure that kind of proves
I don't have what it takes.

706
00:48:16,867 --> 00:48:20,257
Rico, your call's going through.

707
00:48:20,347 --> 00:48:22,144
Take it there.

708
00:48:27,987 --> 00:48:32,105
- Hello? Oh, Johnny!
- Hi, Mom.

709
00:48:32,187 --> 00:48:34,143
B-Bill, pick it up.
It's Johnny!

710
00:48:34,227 --> 00:48:35,945
-Johnny?
- Dad.

711
00:48:36,027 --> 00:48:37,346
- Where's your uniform?
- Bill.

712
00:48:39,107 --> 00:48:40,938
It's just good
to hear from you.

713
00:48:41,027 --> 00:48:43,222
How are you, son?

714
00:48:43,307 --> 00:48:45,457
It's not really working out
here for me, Dad.

715
00:48:45,547 --> 00:48:46,980
I was thinking--

716
00:48:47,067 --> 00:48:48,898
I was hoping it would be
all right if I came home.

717
00:48:48,987 --> 00:48:51,899
Well, of-of course. You should
come home immediately.

718
00:48:53,267 --> 00:48:55,417
I'm sorry.
I've been an idiot.

719
00:48:55,507 --> 00:48:57,702
Don't talk like that.
You just come on home...

720
00:48:57,787 --> 00:48:58,936
talk things out.

721
00:49:00,467 --> 00:49:01,741
We love you, son.

722
00:49:03,187 --> 00:49:05,655
- My, what's that?
- Looks like rain.

723
00:49:05,747 --> 00:49:08,307
- This time of year?
- Sure is dark.

724
00:49:08,387 --> 00:49:10,025
Your transmission
has been terminated...

725
00:49:10,107 --> 00:49:12,541
due to atmospheric
interference.

726
00:49:12,627 --> 00:49:14,026
Please try your call
again later.

727
00:49:17,107 --> 00:49:18,381
Sanchez!

728
00:49:20,467 --> 00:49:21,980
Well, see ya.

729
00:49:22,067 --> 00:49:25,343
Hey, you take that stroll
down Washout Lane...

730
00:49:25,427 --> 00:49:27,179
you're only proving
one thing,Johnny.

731
00:49:27,267 --> 00:49:28,541
What's that, Diz?

732
00:49:31,987 --> 00:49:34,706
That you don't have what
it takes to be a citizen.

733
00:49:38,707 --> 00:49:40,857
Mobile Infantry
is passing by

734
00:49:40,947 --> 00:49:42,778
Mobile Infantry
is passing by

735
00:49:42,867 --> 00:49:45,017
- Well, sound off
- MI

736
00:49:45,107 --> 00:49:47,257
- Sound off
- Passing by

737
00:49:47,347 --> 00:49:50,145
- Count now
- One, two, three, four

738
00:49:50,227 --> 00:49:52,536
- That's it! That's it!
- Left. Left.

739
00:49:52,627 --> 00:49:55,266
- Left, right, left.
- Do you get me?

740
00:49:55,347 --> 00:49:58,464
- Sir, yes, sir!
- I can't hear you!
- What's going on, you guys?

741
00:49:58,547 --> 00:49:59,821
Move, move, move!

742
00:50:02,387 --> 00:50:03,820
What's happening?

743
00:50:09,267 --> 00:50:10,620
Hey, hey, what's going on?

744
00:50:10,707 --> 00:50:12,379
Wh-What's going on?

745
00:50:12,467 --> 00:50:15,903
- Hey, Kitten, what's going on?
- It's war! We're going to war!

746
00:50:20,147 --> 00:50:23,617
The devastation we are seeing
is unparalleled.

747
00:50:23,707 --> 00:50:28,383
Judging from early estimates,
millions dead, a city in ruins.

748
00:50:28,467 --> 00:50:30,458
Is that Geneva?

749
00:50:30,547 --> 00:50:32,299
Goddam bugs whacked us,
Johnny.

750
00:50:32,387 --> 00:50:35,584
The meteor was shot out
of orbit by bug plasma...

751
00:50:35,667 --> 00:50:38,943
that derived from Klendathu,
the Arachnids'home planet.

752
00:50:46,387 --> 00:50:50,699
Nothing lives in what was once
called the Latin Paradise.

753
00:50:50,787 --> 00:50:52,061
Oh,Johnny, it's us.

754
00:50:52,147 --> 00:50:55,503
Buenos Aires has been
wiped off the Earth.

755
00:51:00,067 --> 00:51:01,580
That's home.

756
00:51:03,987 --> 00:51:06,865
The Federal Council met moments
ago and voted unanimously...

757
00:51:06,947 --> 00:51:10,622
for mobilization to destroy
the Arachnid threat.

758
00:51:17,147 --> 00:51:19,183
- I'm serious. I'll go anywhere.
- Forget it, Zim. We need you here.

759
00:51:19,267 --> 00:51:22,065
-I want combat, sir.
-The only way you're gonna see combat...

760
00:51:22,147 --> 00:51:23,978
is if you bust yourself
to private!

761
00:51:24,067 --> 00:51:26,945
- Get me?
- Yes, sir, I get you.

762
00:51:27,027 --> 00:51:30,019
- Sir!
- What do you want, Rico?

763
00:51:30,107 --> 00:51:33,019
I wish to reconsider
my request to drop out, sir.

764
00:51:33,107 --> 00:51:35,098
You already signed
your 1240-A, son.

765
00:51:35,187 --> 00:51:38,702
- It wouldn't be legal.
- Major, I know it was wrong.

766
00:51:38,787 --> 00:51:41,426
I didn't learn from one mistake,
and I made another, sir.

767
00:51:41,507 --> 00:51:43,338
You made your decision, son.

768
00:51:43,427 --> 00:51:47,864
Sir, my family, my whole family,
was in Buenos Aires, sir.

769
00:51:50,707 --> 00:51:53,665
Is this your signature, Rico?

770
00:51:53,747 --> 00:51:55,339
Sir, yes, it is, sir!

771
00:51:59,867 --> 00:52:02,461
Doesn't look like it to me.

772
00:52:05,107 --> 00:52:08,861
- Carry on, Private!
- Yes, sir!

773
00:52:20,426 --> 00:52:25,261
Out of the ashes of Buenos Aires
comes first sorrow...

774
00:52:25,346 --> 00:52:26,904
then anger.

775
00:52:26,986 --> 00:52:29,819
The only good bug
is a dead bug.

776
00:52:29,906 --> 00:52:32,864
In Geneva,
the Federal Council convenes.

777
00:52:32,946 --> 00:52:36,495
We must meet the threat
with our valour, our blood...

778
00:52:36,586 --> 00:52:38,702
indeed, with our very lives...

779
00:52:38,786 --> 00:52:43,177
to ensure that human civilization,
not insect...

780
00:52:43,266 --> 00:52:46,975
dominates this galaxy,
now and always!

781
00:52:48,226 --> 00:52:49,739
Sky Marshal Dienes
announces plans...

782
00:52:49,826 --> 00:52:51,703
for an offensive
against Klendathu...

783
00:52:51,786 --> 00:52:55,017
source of the bug meteor
that destroyed Buenos Aires.

784
00:52:57,546 --> 00:53:01,778
Every day, Federal scientists
are looking for new ways to kill bugs.

785
00:53:01,866 --> 00:53:04,141
Your basic Arachnid warrior
isn't too smart...

786
00:53:04,226 --> 00:53:05,500
but you can
blow off a limb...

787
00:53:08,226 --> 00:53:10,694
and it's still 86 percent
combat effective.

788
00:53:10,786 --> 00:53:14,381
Here's a tip.:Aim for the nerve stem,
and put it down for good.

789
00:53:20,866 --> 00:53:23,858
Everyone's doing their part. Are you?

790
00:53:25,866 --> 00:53:28,300
- Die! Die!
- The war effort needs your effort...

791
00:53:28,386 --> 00:53:30,581
at work, at home,
in your community.

792
00:53:34,346 --> 00:53:35,984
We now break net and take you live...

793
00:53:36,066 --> 00:53:38,261
to Fleet Battle Station Ticonderoga...

794
00:53:38,346 --> 00:53:40,780
deep inside
the Arachnid Quarantine Zone...

795
00:53:40,866 --> 00:53:45,257
where the men and women of the Federal
Armed Services prepare to attack.

796
00:53:45,346 --> 00:53:49,100
D XQ uplink on two, one.
You're on.

797
00:53:49,186 --> 00:53:51,336
No one here in the AQZ
knows exactly...

798
00:53:51,426 --> 00:53:53,576
when the invasion
of Klendathu will occur.

799
00:53:53,666 --> 00:53:55,338
But everyone's
talking about it...

800
00:53:55,426 --> 00:53:57,257
and the talk says tomorrow.

801
00:53:57,346 --> 00:54:00,144
Here's a bunch of MI kids that look
like they could eat bugs for lunch.

802
00:54:00,226 --> 00:54:02,057
- Yum, yum, yum.
- So, trooper,

803
00:54:02,146 --> 00:54:03,818
you're not too worried
about fighting the Arachnids?

804
00:54:03,906 --> 00:54:06,466
Hey, shoot a nuke down a bug hole,
you got a lot of dead bugs.

805
00:54:06,546 --> 00:54:09,504
-Am I right?
- I just hope it's not over
before we get some.

806
00:54:09,586 --> 00:54:11,338
- Okay, come on.
- Some say the bugs were provoked...

807
00:54:11,426 --> 00:54:13,986
by the intrusion of humans
into their natural habitat...

808
00:54:14,066 --> 00:54:17,900
that a "live and let live policy"
is preferable to war with the bugs.

809
00:54:17,986 --> 00:54:19,339
Let me tell you something.

810
00:54:19,426 --> 00:54:21,417
I'm from Buenos Aires,
and I say kill them all!

811
00:54:21,506 --> 00:54:22,780
- Yeah!
- Go on, trooper!
- Yeah!

812
00:54:22,866 --> 00:54:24,219
- Yeah!
- Oh, yeah!

813
00:54:24,306 --> 00:54:26,137
Big bad bugs, huh?

814
00:54:26,226 --> 00:54:28,217
Hey, guys,
we ought to get tattoos.

815
00:54:28,306 --> 00:54:29,580
- Hey, let's all get cut together.
- Yeah.

816
00:54:29,666 --> 00:54:30,940
- What do I want a tattoo for?
- Oh, what?

817
00:54:31,026 --> 00:54:32,539
Your skin's too pretty?
Come on, everybody's doing it.

818
00:54:32,626 --> 00:54:33,900
Hey,Johnny!

819
00:54:36,146 --> 00:54:37,420
Johnny Rico.

820
00:54:39,666 --> 00:54:40,940
Carmen?

821
00:54:43,786 --> 00:54:45,981
Oh. At ease.

822
00:54:46,066 --> 00:54:48,978
Guess I ought to lose the hat
when I'm off duty.

823
00:54:49,066 --> 00:54:53,139
- Hi, Diz.
- Carmen.

824
00:54:55,306 --> 00:54:57,820
My mother was right about you.

825
00:54:57,906 --> 00:54:59,658
You look great in a uniform.

826
00:54:59,746 --> 00:55:01,577
You look pretty good yourself.

827
00:55:03,386 --> 00:55:05,217
So, what do you hear?

828
00:55:05,306 --> 00:55:08,139
You know about anyone
who made it out of BA alive?

829
00:55:08,226 --> 00:55:10,694
Most of the time
I don't think about it.

830
00:55:10,786 --> 00:55:12,344
Like it happened
to someone else.

831
00:55:12,426 --> 00:55:16,465
Then it hits me,
and I, uh, can't stop crying.

832
00:55:16,546 --> 00:55:20,141
Well, we're still alive.
Got to be happy about that.

833
00:55:20,226 --> 00:55:23,377
You don't look
very happy to see me.

834
00:55:23,466 --> 00:55:25,741
Should I be?

835
00:55:25,826 --> 00:55:30,377
Johnny, it's different now.
We're at war.

836
00:55:30,466 --> 00:55:34,379
I mean, I think what I did was
probably the best thing for both of us.

837
00:55:34,466 --> 00:55:36,536
Everything copacetic,
Lieutenant?

838
00:55:37,506 --> 00:55:39,815
Zander, you remember Johnny.

839
00:55:39,906 --> 00:55:42,056
Zander and I
are a flight team now.

840
00:55:42,146 --> 00:55:43,818
Yeah, and we're best in the fleet.

841
00:55:45,186 --> 00:55:46,778
I get it.

842
00:55:46,866 --> 00:55:49,585
This is the part that's
best for both of us.

843
00:55:49,666 --> 00:55:52,134
- Don't do me any more favours.
-Johnny, wait.

844
00:55:52,226 --> 00:55:54,376
No, forget it, Lieutenant.
He's Mobile Infantry.

845
00:55:54,466 --> 00:55:56,297
See, when you're
trained to kill...

846
00:55:56,386 --> 00:55:58,695
it just doesn't pay
to be polite.

847
00:55:58,786 --> 00:56:00,936
You got something to say
about the Mobile Infantry?

848
00:56:01,026 --> 00:56:03,779
I think you heard me.

849
00:56:03,866 --> 00:56:06,778
You want to make
something of it, Private?

850
00:56:08,506 --> 00:56:10,656
Not with an officer.
No, sir.

851
00:56:10,746 --> 00:56:14,341
- The MI doesn't mint stupid troopers.
- Well, let's disregard rank.

852
00:56:14,426 --> 00:56:16,576
- Zander, please.
- Let it go, Rico.
- Let it go.

853
00:56:16,666 --> 00:56:19,976
Everybody hear that?
Rank is not an issue here.

854
00:56:20,066 --> 00:56:22,944
- Don't do this.
- Come on. What's he gonna do?

855
00:56:36,306 --> 00:56:38,740
Come on, jarheads!

856
00:56:38,826 --> 00:56:40,578
Let go of me! Come on!
I'm gonna kill you!

857
00:56:42,186 --> 00:56:45,974
I'm gonna kill you!
I'll kill you!

858
00:56:46,066 --> 00:56:47,579
- Guys! Guys! Quit it!
- Come on! Come on!

859
00:56:47,666 --> 00:56:49,019
- He's not worth it!
- Come on!
- Come on!

860
00:56:49,106 --> 00:56:50,744
- Let's get--
- Come on!

861
00:56:50,826 --> 00:56:54,421
Forget it, Rico! Mobile Infantry
and Fleet don't mix. Come on.

862
00:56:56,586 --> 00:56:58,178
Come on, let's go.

863
00:57:00,226 --> 00:57:01,545
Jarheads.

864
00:57:03,906 --> 00:57:06,545
- Mobile Infantry rules!
- Yeah!

865
00:57:06,626 --> 00:57:08,582
Oh, God, that hurts.

866
00:57:08,666 --> 00:57:11,624
Hey, well, I got something that might
hurt just a little bit more, buddy.

867
00:57:13,186 --> 00:57:16,462
Oh, yeah! We're gonna fight,
and we're gonna win!

868
00:57:16,546 --> 00:57:18,662
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

869
00:57:33,506 --> 00:57:35,178
This is the captain speaking.

870
00:57:35,266 --> 00:57:37,382
All personnel
prepare for drop.

871
00:57:37,466 --> 00:57:39,775
We are at D-minus three
and counting.

872
00:57:50,786 --> 00:57:53,744
We are going in
with first wave.

873
00:57:53,826 --> 00:57:55,862
Means more bugs
for us to kill.

874
00:57:55,946 --> 00:57:57,379
You smash the entire area.

875
00:57:57,466 --> 00:57:59,457
You kill anything that has
more than two legs.

876
00:57:59,546 --> 00:58:01,935
- You get me?
- We get you, sir!

877
00:58:48,026 --> 00:58:50,745
-Plasma, ma'am, from the planet.
-Bug batteries.

878
00:58:50,826 --> 00:58:53,545
According to military intelligence,
it'll be random and light.

879
00:58:55,146 --> 00:58:57,614
- Drop status?
- Drop is...

880
00:58:57,706 --> 00:58:59,697
35 percent complete, ma'am.

881
00:59:04,986 --> 00:59:06,339
Steady as she goes,
Number Two.

882
00:59:18,266 --> 00:59:22,817
Remember your training,
and you will make it back alive!

883
00:59:39,946 --> 00:59:42,744
This isn't random or light.
Someone made a mistake.

884
00:59:42,826 --> 00:59:44,578
That's it.
We're empty, ma'am.

885
00:59:54,226 --> 00:59:55,944
Someone made
a big goddam mistake!

886
01:00:02,826 --> 01:00:04,498
Break for high orbit!

887
01:00:41,866 --> 01:00:43,140
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

888
01:00:48,146 --> 01:00:49,659
Johnny!

889
01:01:10,186 --> 01:01:12,859
- Rockets up!
- Rocket crew, move up!

890
01:01:35,866 --> 01:01:38,664
- Nuke 'em! Levy! Rico!
- Heat 'em up!

891
01:01:43,226 --> 01:01:45,945
- Set.
- Fire!

892
01:01:46,666 --> 01:01:47,781
Down!

893
01:01:52,386 --> 01:01:54,581
- Follow me!
- Let's go!

894
01:01:57,506 --> 01:02:00,418
First platoon, left flank!

895
01:02:00,506 --> 01:02:04,465
Split up! First and
second squads, follow me.

896
01:02:04,546 --> 01:02:07,219
Two, cover!
One, with me!

897
01:02:08,106 --> 01:02:09,937
Along side! Side to side!

898
01:02:11,586 --> 01:02:12,701
Fire!

899
01:02:30,346 --> 01:02:32,098
Here they come!

900
01:02:35,306 --> 01:02:37,695
- Ace, what are we doing?
- Uh, I don't know.

901
01:02:42,426 --> 01:02:46,783
- I don't know.
- Kill them! Kill them all!

902
01:02:52,986 --> 01:02:54,738
Come on!

903
01:02:56,786 --> 01:02:59,584
Come on! Come on!
You want some?

904
01:03:00,466 --> 01:03:02,457
Here's some! Yeah!

905
01:03:02,546 --> 01:03:03,865
Here's some of this!

906
01:03:07,186 --> 01:03:09,177
Oh, my God!

907
01:03:09,266 --> 01:03:11,575
Shujimi!

908
01:03:11,666 --> 01:03:13,622
No, no, no!

909
01:03:15,786 --> 01:03:17,458
Help! Help! Help!

910
01:03:19,786 --> 01:03:21,981
No! God!

911
01:03:27,146 --> 01:03:29,182
Let's get out of here!

912
01:03:31,706 --> 01:03:33,458
Fall back!

913
01:03:56,906 --> 01:03:59,215
Mayday!

914
01:03:59,306 --> 01:04:01,297
-All units,
- What's going on?
- fall back to retrieval.

915
01:04:01,386 --> 01:04:02,739
- Repeat.
- You got com?
-All units...

916
01:04:02,826 --> 01:04:04,498
- fall back to retrieval.
- It's a general retreat!

917
01:04:04,586 --> 01:04:06,577
- Back to the boats!
- Come on!

918
01:04:06,666 --> 01:04:07,940
Come on, let's go!

919
01:04:09,866 --> 01:04:11,379
We've just landed here
on what cap troopers...

920
01:04:11,466 --> 01:04:13,457
are calling Big K...

921
01:04:13,546 --> 01:04:15,935
with the 6th Mobile
Infantry Division.

922
01:04:16,026 --> 01:04:18,904
It's an ugly planet,
a bug planet.

923
01:04:18,986 --> 01:04:20,977
A planet hostile
to life as we--

924
01:04:26,266 --> 01:04:27,699
Help me!

925
01:04:31,706 --> 01:04:32,980
Squad right!

926
01:04:44,506 --> 01:04:47,145
Come on! Go, go, go!

927
01:04:47,226 --> 01:04:48,818
Get out of here now!

928
01:04:50,346 --> 01:04:52,416
- Watch your step!
- Watch your flank! Watch your flank!

929
01:04:52,506 --> 01:04:54,258
GXR, we're being overrun.

930
01:05:03,786 --> 01:05:05,936
Kitten, no!

931
01:05:35,786 --> 01:05:37,139
Oh, God!

932
01:05:37,226 --> 01:05:41,139
Oh, God! Oh! Oh!

933
01:06:09,226 --> 01:06:10,818
Crisis for humankind.

934
01:06:10,906 --> 01:06:13,136
Fleet officials admit
they underestimated...

935
01:06:13,226 --> 01:06:16,502
the Arachnids'
defensive capability.

936
01:06:16,586 --> 01:06:19,054
Accepting responsibility
for Klendathu...

937
01:06:19,146 --> 01:06:21,614
Sky Marshal Dienes resigns.

938
01:06:21,706 --> 01:06:24,174
His successor,
Sky Marshal Tahat Meru...

939
01:06:24,266 --> 01:06:26,734
outlines her new strategy.

940
01:06:26,826 --> 01:06:28,657
To fight the bug...

941
01:06:28,746 --> 01:06:31,055
we must understand the bug.

942
01:06:31,146 --> 01:06:34,138
We can ill afford
another Klendathu.

943
01:06:36,546 --> 01:06:38,537
Federal scientists
struggle to explain...

944
01:06:38,626 --> 01:06:41,345
the intelligent military actions
of the Arachnids.

945
01:06:41,426 --> 01:06:43,417
When a colony reaches
a certain size...

946
01:06:43,506 --> 01:06:46,100
300 generations or something,
it gets smarter.

947
01:06:46,186 --> 01:06:47,505
- Insects with intelligence?
- Now, wait--

948
01:06:47,586 --> 01:06:49,258
Have you ever met one?
I can't believe...

949
01:06:49,346 --> 01:06:51,177
- I am hearing this nonsense.
- Would you just wait a moment?

950
01:06:51,266 --> 01:06:54,099
- This is the most ridiculous
conversation I have ever had.
- Maybe-- Maybe...

951
01:06:54,186 --> 01:06:57,735
there is some kind of bug
that we haven't seen yet.:

952
01:06:57,826 --> 01:07:00,135
a leadership caste,
a-a hive brain.

953
01:07:00,226 --> 01:07:04,697
Brain Bugs? Frankly, I find the idea
of a bug that thinks offensive!

954
01:07:18,146 --> 01:07:21,661
Ticonderoga, this is Rodger Young
requesting approach vector.

955
01:07:21,746 --> 01:07:23,498
Affirmative, Rodger Young.

956
01:07:23,586 --> 01:07:26,259
One-zero-zero-niner-five-two.

957
01:07:26,346 --> 01:07:27,461
Welcome back.

958
01:07:29,666 --> 01:07:30,940
My God.

959
01:07:32,786 --> 01:07:34,777
How could this happen?

960
01:07:34,866 --> 01:07:37,141
We thought we were smarter
than the bugs.

961
01:07:53,746 --> 01:07:55,543
Give me something, please!

962
01:07:56,626 --> 01:07:57,945
It hurts!

963
01:08:03,026 --> 01:08:04,345
Be right with you.

964
01:08:06,706 --> 01:08:08,025
Help me.

965
01:08:14,706 --> 01:08:17,174
It's strange. There's
almost no wounded at all.

966
01:08:17,266 --> 01:08:19,222
Bugs don't take prisoners.

967
01:08:27,946 --> 01:08:29,265
Oh, no.

968
01:08:30,666 --> 01:08:31,940
Look.

969
01:08:36,266 --> 01:08:38,336
- Carmen--
- See it? Right there.

970
01:09:59,746 --> 01:10:02,385
- There he is.
- Come on, we'll just wake him up.

971
01:10:02,466 --> 01:10:06,698
Hey,Johnny! Hey!

972
01:10:06,786 --> 01:10:09,584
- Hey, Rico!
- Hey,Johnny!

973
01:10:09,666 --> 01:10:11,497
- Hey, Rico!
- Wake up!
- How you doin', fish boy?

974
01:10:11,586 --> 01:10:14,054
Hey, look.
You're dead!

975
01:10:14,146 --> 01:10:16,341
Killed in action!

976
01:10:18,626 --> 01:10:20,457
- Three more days.
- Three days.

977
01:10:20,546 --> 01:10:22,457
- And you're out.
- Good as new. See you later.

978
01:10:22,546 --> 01:10:23,820
Bye.

979
01:10:51,826 --> 01:10:53,498
So what do you hear
about our new unit?

980
01:10:53,586 --> 01:10:55,895
Roughnecks killed more bugs
than any other outfit on Big K.

981
01:10:55,986 --> 01:10:58,705
Yeah, well, I hear their
lieutenant's a real nutbuster.

982
01:11:01,586 --> 01:11:03,178
Who's top kick?

983
01:11:05,586 --> 01:11:07,178
You want the job, huh?

984
01:11:07,266 --> 01:11:08,540
I wouldn't mind.

985
01:11:08,626 --> 01:11:10,423
I would.

986
01:11:11,826 --> 01:11:13,100
Just doing my part.

987
01:11:13,186 --> 01:11:14,585
Orders.

988
01:11:17,106 --> 01:11:18,459
Yours?

989
01:11:18,546 --> 01:11:20,218
Where you been
besides Big K?

990
01:11:20,306 --> 01:11:24,015
- Outer rings, Zegema Beach.
- Zegema Beach?

991
01:11:24,106 --> 01:11:26,381
- I always wanted to go there.
- Good luck.

992
01:11:26,466 --> 01:11:31,335
- It's not there any more.
- So, I hear your lieutenant's
a real nutbuster.

993
01:11:34,306 --> 01:11:36,945
No one talks about
the lieutenant that way.

994
01:11:37,026 --> 01:11:39,381
- He saved my life.
- Mine too.

995
01:11:40,706 --> 01:11:42,503
- Same for me.
- Me too.

996
01:11:44,226 --> 01:11:47,024
Well, sounds like
he's quite a guy.

997
01:11:47,106 --> 01:11:48,698
Who do you think
saved your ass?

998
01:11:49,826 --> 01:11:53,136
Stand by.
Attention on deck!

999
01:12:05,026 --> 01:12:07,017
This is for you new people.

1000
01:12:07,106 --> 01:12:09,062
I only have one rule:

1001
01:12:09,146 --> 01:12:12,377
Everyone fights.
No one quits.

1002
01:12:12,466 --> 01:12:15,344
You don't do your job,
I'll shoot you.

1003
01:12:15,426 --> 01:12:16,620
Do you get me?

1004
01:12:16,706 --> 01:12:18,617
We get you, sir!

1005
01:12:20,266 --> 01:12:22,575
- Welcome to the Roughnecks.
- Rasczak's Roughnecks!

1006
01:12:23,786 --> 01:12:25,777
At ease. Listen up.

1007
01:12:25,866 --> 01:12:29,302
We got a new Sky Marshal
and a new battle plan.

1008
01:12:29,386 --> 01:12:31,695
We're gonna clean out the
systems outlying Klendathu...

1009
01:12:31,786 --> 01:12:33,856
one planet at a time.

1010
01:12:33,946 --> 01:12:36,016
Tomorrow
we hit Tango Urilla.

1011
01:12:36,106 --> 01:12:40,338
After Fleet glasses
the planet, MI mops up.

1012
01:12:40,426 --> 01:12:41,620
Carry on.

1013
01:13:29,826 --> 01:13:32,294
All right.
Spread out!

1014
01:13:32,386 --> 01:13:35,901
Fire teams! You locate
a bug hole, nuke it.

1015
01:13:43,426 --> 01:13:45,257
Watkins, shake out
Flores and Rico.

1016
01:13:45,346 --> 01:13:47,576
Copy that.
Move out!

1017
01:13:47,666 --> 01:13:50,385
First platoon,
we're going for that ridge.

1018
01:13:50,466 --> 01:13:53,264
- Levy, you're with me.
- No, I'm in A Squad.
I'm going with Rico.

1019
01:13:53,346 --> 01:13:54,779
Shut up and follow me!

1020
01:14:31,626 --> 01:14:33,378
Hey, you like that?

1021
01:14:33,466 --> 01:14:35,377
Fungus-sucking sack
of maggot puke!

1022
01:14:35,466 --> 01:14:36,979
It's dead, Watkins!
It's dead!

1023
01:14:41,906 --> 01:14:44,056
Ain't much to look at after
you scrape them off your boot.

1024
01:14:45,546 --> 01:14:48,185
Bug hole. There.

1025
01:15:02,346 --> 01:15:03,461
Nuke 'em, Rico!

1026
01:15:09,226 --> 01:15:10,625
Fire in the hole!

1027
01:15:21,866 --> 01:15:24,175
Watkins, we're under
heavy attack. Position M-4.

1028
01:15:24,266 --> 01:15:26,416
- Get over here!
- Move!

1029
01:15:36,106 --> 01:15:38,984
- You got a bug problem, ma'am?
- Ah, stow it, trooper!

1030
01:15:59,666 --> 01:16:01,657
Tanker!

1031
01:16:01,746 --> 01:16:04,704
- Oh, shit!
- Come on! Move!

1032
01:16:13,066 --> 01:16:14,897
Get down!

1033
01:16:22,706 --> 01:16:23,855
Come on!

1034
01:17:29,386 --> 01:17:31,377
Stay down, sucker!

1035
01:17:31,466 --> 01:17:33,297
- Gillespie.
- Well done!

1036
01:17:33,386 --> 01:17:34,899
Call for retrieval.

1037
01:17:34,986 --> 01:17:37,944
- Medic!
- Nice moves.

1038
01:17:38,026 --> 01:17:40,176
Where'd you learn how
to do that, soldier?

1039
01:17:40,266 --> 01:17:43,224
Back in school, sir.
Don't you remember?

1040
01:17:43,306 --> 01:17:47,140
- I was captain of the team.
- Rico?

1041
01:17:47,226 --> 01:17:49,865
- Sir.
- I need a corporal.

1042
01:17:49,946 --> 01:17:53,382
You're it until you're dead
or till I find somebody better.

1043
01:17:54,266 --> 01:17:56,177
Thank you, sir.

1044
01:17:56,266 --> 01:17:58,826
- All right, saddle up! Show's over.
- Way to go, Corporal.

1045
01:17:58,906 --> 01:18:04,026
- Hey, I need a squad leader.
- Oh, no. No, I've been there
and blew it.

1046
01:18:04,106 --> 01:18:05,459
I'm just here to fight.

1047
01:18:06,706 --> 01:18:08,776
What about it, Diz?

1048
01:18:08,866 --> 01:18:11,016
First sergeant,
get your gear in section--

1049
01:18:11,106 --> 01:18:12,664
Looks like
I'm your girl, sir.

1050
01:18:17,386 --> 01:18:18,944
- Catch you later.
- All right.

1051
01:18:24,706 --> 01:18:26,503
Listen up!

1052
01:18:26,586 --> 01:18:29,658
I expect the best,
and I give the best!

1053
01:18:33,346 --> 01:18:34,620
Here's the beer!

1054
01:18:38,506 --> 01:18:40,383
Here's the entertainment!

1055
01:18:44,706 --> 01:18:46,617
Have fun!
That's an order!

1056
01:18:47,666 --> 01:18:49,179
This one's for me!

1057
01:18:50,546 --> 01:18:52,059
Thank you, Lieutenant!

1058
01:18:55,626 --> 01:18:56,900
Rico!

1059
01:18:58,306 --> 01:19:00,297
You kill bugs good.

1060
01:19:00,386 --> 01:19:01,660
Thanks.

1061
01:19:03,426 --> 01:19:05,656
You knew the lieutenant
before the war.

1062
01:19:05,746 --> 01:19:07,577
What was he like?

1063
01:19:07,666 --> 01:19:10,624
He was a teacher.
Kind of like he knew it all.

1064
01:19:10,706 --> 01:19:12,697
He always had
this little smile.

1065
01:19:12,786 --> 01:19:16,062
Yeah, well, he don't
smile much any more.

1066
01:19:16,146 --> 01:19:19,741
Yeah, well, I guess your bottle fills up
real quick when your kids get smeared.

1067
01:19:19,826 --> 01:19:22,181
- Come on, Corporal.
- Ah, nah, I don't do that any more.

1068
01:19:22,266 --> 01:19:24,655
I remember when you used to dance.
Come on.

1069
01:19:24,746 --> 01:19:26,099
Do I have to pull rank?

1070
01:19:28,786 --> 01:19:30,265
Excuse me, sir.

1071
01:19:38,706 --> 01:19:43,575
Rico. You once asked me
for advice. Want some now?

1072
01:19:43,666 --> 01:19:46,260
- Yes, sir.
- Lieutenant, HQ is on the com.

1073
01:19:48,626 --> 01:19:50,582
Never pass up a good thing.

1074
01:19:59,186 --> 01:20:01,700
Watkins. Beer?

1075
01:20:13,386 --> 01:20:14,660
Ace.

1076
01:20:23,306 --> 01:20:25,774
So, Rico, what are you
doing after the dance?

1077
01:21:11,466 --> 01:21:12,785
What's so funny?

1078
01:21:14,266 --> 01:21:16,336
You know, just the way
things work out.

1079
01:21:33,146 --> 01:21:35,535
We finally
got together, Diz.

1080
01:21:38,586 --> 01:21:40,019
I love you,Johnny.

1081
01:21:50,186 --> 01:21:51,380
Rico!

1082
01:21:54,026 --> 01:21:56,745
We're moving out.
There's been a distress call
from General Owen on Planet P.

1083
01:21:56,826 --> 01:21:58,896
So get your shit wired
and report in ten minutes.

1084
01:21:58,986 --> 01:22:00,339
Yes, sir.

1085
01:22:00,426 --> 01:22:01,859
Who's that with you?

1086
01:22:05,306 --> 01:22:07,297
Flores, sir.

1087
01:22:08,426 --> 01:22:10,417
Make it 20 minutes.

1088
01:22:10,506 --> 01:22:11,621
Yes, sir.

1089
01:22:12,826 --> 01:22:14,100
Twenty minutes?

1090
01:22:15,226 --> 01:22:16,500
We can do it.

1091
01:22:53,306 --> 01:22:54,898
Whiskey Outpost,
do you copy?

1092
01:22:54,986 --> 01:22:57,898
This is Roughneck 2-0
on tac three. Come in, please.

1093
01:22:59,146 --> 01:23:00,499
Whiskey Outpost,
Whiskey Outpost,

1094
01:23:00,586 --> 01:23:02,736
this is Roughneck 2-0
on tac three.

1095
01:23:02,826 --> 01:23:04,976
- Any contact with General Owen?
- No, sir.

1096
01:23:05,066 --> 01:23:06,419
Not even
the transponder signal.

1097
01:23:06,506 --> 01:23:09,782
It's these canyons.
Go to higher ground, Sergeant.

1098
01:23:15,506 --> 01:23:17,303
Whiskey Outpost,
Whiskey Outpost...

1099
01:23:17,386 --> 01:23:19,138
this is Roughneck 2-0 on--

1100
01:23:22,346 --> 01:23:24,018
Look out!

1101
01:23:30,746 --> 01:23:32,304
Sugar, your weapon.

1102
01:23:38,826 --> 01:23:40,942
Help me! Help me!

1103
01:23:50,826 --> 01:23:54,262
I'd expect anyone in this unit
to do the same for me.

1104
01:23:55,586 --> 01:23:57,258
- Rico.
- Sir.

1105
01:23:57,346 --> 01:23:59,257
You're acting sergeant.
Move 'em out.

1106
01:24:00,586 --> 01:24:03,339
You heard the lieutenant!
Saddle up!

1107
01:24:53,026 --> 01:24:56,257
Jeez, someone really
humped the bunk.

1108
01:24:56,346 --> 01:24:58,462
- Watkins.
- Sir.

1109
01:24:58,546 --> 01:25:00,776
Secure this compound.
Police these bodies.

1110
01:25:00,866 --> 01:25:03,903
Yes, sir. Give me three
up on the tower, now!

1111
01:25:03,986 --> 01:25:05,863
- Aye-aye.
- OP there! OP there!

1112
01:25:05,946 --> 01:25:08,506
- Away!
- Number Two, police up these bodies!

1113
01:25:08,586 --> 01:25:10,463
- Stinks in there.
- Second squad,
come with me on the gate!

1114
01:25:10,546 --> 01:25:12,696
- Rico!
- Churchill, come with me!
- Yes, sir.

1115
01:25:12,786 --> 01:25:14,299
We need retrieval.
This place crawls.

1116
01:25:14,386 --> 01:25:16,536
Get somebody in the communications tent
and get me an uplink.

1117
01:25:16,626 --> 01:25:18,423
Yes, sir.
Diz, check it out.

1118
01:25:18,506 --> 01:25:19,859
- Roger.
- Command group with me.

1119
01:25:24,306 --> 01:25:25,500
Ah, shit.

1120
01:25:25,586 --> 01:25:26,905
Lieutenant!

1121
01:25:29,266 --> 01:25:32,338
Dirty bugs came in right
while they were having chow.

1122
01:25:37,746 --> 01:25:40,499
Yeah, this is
where they got in.

1123
01:25:42,066 --> 01:25:44,216
Lieutenant.

1124
01:25:44,306 --> 01:25:46,900
I think you're gonna
want to see this.

1125
01:25:46,986 --> 01:25:48,499
What do you got, Flores?

1126
01:25:48,586 --> 01:25:50,338
God, I hate this place.

1127
01:26:04,746 --> 01:26:07,101
What does that look like
to you, Rico?

1128
01:26:09,706 --> 01:26:11,458
Looks like a bug was
in his brain, sir.

1129
01:26:20,906 --> 01:26:23,374
They sucked his brains out.

1130
01:26:32,426 --> 01:26:33,700
Open that.

1131
01:26:37,066 --> 01:26:38,818
Officer on the deck!

1132
01:26:38,906 --> 01:26:41,295
- Pick up the general.
- Gone?

1133
01:26:41,386 --> 01:26:42,899
Is it safe? We've got
to get out of here!

1134
01:26:42,986 --> 01:26:45,136
- General!
- We've gotta--
- Sir!

1135
01:26:48,426 --> 01:26:52,101
Thank God for you,
all of you.

1136
01:26:52,186 --> 01:26:55,303
You're all gonna be heroes.
Every last one of you.

1137
01:26:55,386 --> 01:26:57,775
- Close that hole.
- Yes, sir.

1138
01:26:57,866 --> 01:27:00,903
I had to evade capture. The security
of the Federation was at stake.

1139
01:27:00,986 --> 01:27:02,260
Fire in the hole!

1140
01:27:04,666 --> 01:27:07,305
I have operational knowledge
of what we're up to out here.

1141
01:27:07,386 --> 01:27:09,695
- Flores, I need that uplink.
- Working on it, sir.

1142
01:27:09,786 --> 01:27:11,697
- Damn it.
- See?

1143
01:27:11,786 --> 01:27:13,378
- They get in your mind.
- Battlegroup, this is Roughneck 2-0.

1144
01:27:13,466 --> 01:27:14,979
- Look, they did it to Farley.
- Do you read?

1145
01:27:15,066 --> 01:27:17,057
- They got in his mind.
- Come in, Battlegroup.
This is Roughneck 2-0.

1146
01:27:17,146 --> 01:27:20,104
They make you do things.
They made Farley call headquarters.

1147
01:27:20,186 --> 01:27:21,858
The distress call was a trap.

1148
01:27:21,946 --> 01:27:25,177
They're just like us.
They want to know what makes us tick.

1149
01:27:25,266 --> 01:27:27,143
They want to know us,
so they can kill us.

1150
01:27:27,226 --> 01:27:29,057
Roughnecks, this is lead.
Prepare for attack.

1151
01:27:29,146 --> 01:27:31,376
- I repeat, we're gonna be attacked.
- Where's the retrieval boat?

1152
01:27:31,466 --> 01:27:34,264
Mayday. Mayday. This is Roughneck 2-0
to Battlegroup. Do you read?

1153
01:27:34,346 --> 01:27:36,098
- Oh, God!
- Come in, Battlegroup.
This is Roughneck 2-0.

1154
01:27:36,186 --> 01:27:38,984
We're gonna die!
Don't you understand?

1155
01:27:39,066 --> 01:27:40,340
We're all gonna die!

1156
01:27:41,866 --> 01:27:43,219
Second squad, follow me!

1157
01:27:43,306 --> 01:27:46,139
- Control yourself, General.
- I can't.

1158
01:27:46,226 --> 01:27:47,705
I can't.

1159
01:27:47,786 --> 01:27:49,344
I wish you'd just shoot me.

1160
01:27:51,626 --> 01:27:54,902
Lieutenant! He's just a little
out of his mind, sir.

1161
01:27:56,106 --> 01:27:57,937
Bugs! Bugs!

1162
01:27:58,026 --> 01:28:00,176
- Die!
- All right.

1163
01:28:00,266 --> 01:28:03,064
Warm it all up!
Everything you've got!

1164
01:28:03,146 --> 01:28:05,137
- Move!
- Come on, you apes!

1165
01:28:05,226 --> 01:28:06,739
You want to live forever?

1166
01:28:08,946 --> 01:28:10,265
- Here!
- I got bugs!

1167
01:28:39,426 --> 01:28:40,700
Fire at will!

1168
01:29:19,466 --> 01:29:20,819
Incoming!

1169
01:29:37,906 --> 01:29:39,100
Down!

1170
01:29:42,666 --> 01:29:43,860
No! Hey!

1171
01:29:48,626 --> 01:29:51,459
- Watch your fire!
- Watch casualties!

1172
01:29:51,546 --> 01:29:53,662
Rico, where's
my communication?

1173
01:29:53,746 --> 01:29:55,737
- Diz, status on the uplink!
- Give me a minute.

1174
01:29:55,826 --> 01:29:57,623
We don't have a minute!

1175
01:30:06,546 --> 01:30:08,537
Battlegroup, this is Roughneck 2-0.
We are under--

1176
01:30:08,626 --> 01:30:11,584
- This is Rodger Young. Go ahead.
- We are under attack, sir.
We need retrieval now!

1177
01:30:11,666 --> 01:30:13,019
We have Planet Pas clear.

1178
01:30:13,106 --> 01:30:15,097
This place crawls, sir.
We need pickup now!

1179
01:30:15,186 --> 01:30:17,336
-What's your position?
-Come down on this transmission.

1180
01:30:17,426 --> 01:30:18,939
Inside the outpost?
That's crazy!

1181
01:30:19,026 --> 01:30:20,823
Well, I hope you have
a crazy pilot. Out!

1182
01:30:52,066 --> 01:30:53,624
Lieutenant!

1183
01:30:53,706 --> 01:30:55,219
Boat coming down, sir!

1184
01:30:55,306 --> 01:30:58,662
Fall back into the compound!
Fall back!

1185
01:31:22,346 --> 01:31:24,906
Hold here!
Hold what you've got!

1186
01:31:35,146 --> 01:31:36,420
Running low!

1187
01:31:37,706 --> 01:31:39,059
I'm out!

1188
01:31:39,146 --> 01:31:41,296
Here! Make 'em count!

1189
01:31:59,946 --> 01:32:01,777
Make cover fire!
Fall back!

1190
01:32:17,226 --> 01:32:18,898
Move, move, move!

1191
01:32:21,226 --> 01:32:23,615
Fall back to the boat!
Haul ass!

1192
01:32:36,786 --> 01:32:38,742
- Oh, my God!
- Oh!

1193
01:32:42,266 --> 01:32:44,734
- Get him outta there!
- Pull!
- Come on!

1194
01:32:50,666 --> 01:32:52,702
Rico! Rico!

1195
01:32:54,026 --> 01:32:57,143
- You know what to do!
- Yes, sir!

1196
01:33:01,706 --> 01:33:03,219
Do it, Rico!

1197
01:33:27,466 --> 01:33:29,934
- Yeah!
- Dizzy!

1198
01:33:50,906 --> 01:33:52,578
No!

1199
01:33:52,666 --> 01:33:55,339
Ace, help me!
Hold her down!

1200
01:34:00,106 --> 01:34:02,176
Move!
Get her into the boat!

1201
01:34:03,706 --> 01:34:05,424
Come on, Diz!
Don't die on me!

1202
01:34:05,506 --> 01:34:06,734
Let's get her out!
Let's go, let's go!

1203
01:34:12,906 --> 01:34:14,544
Let's go! Get aboard!

1204
01:34:16,106 --> 01:34:17,903
Tower, let's go!

1205
01:34:23,786 --> 01:34:27,540
Let's move it, tower!
Run!

1206
01:34:33,346 --> 01:34:34,665
Lift off!

1207
01:35:04,026 --> 01:35:08,304
-Johnny, I'm dying-dying.
- No.

1208
01:35:08,386 --> 01:35:10,456
You're gonna be
all right, Diz.

1209
01:35:10,546 --> 01:35:13,583
It's all right...

1210
01:35:13,666 --> 01:35:16,021
because I got to have you.

1211
01:35:23,186 --> 01:35:25,142
Johnny, don't let me go!

1212
01:35:25,226 --> 01:35:26,898
Joh--Joh--

1213
01:35:26,986 --> 01:35:28,897
Don't let--
Don't let--

1214
01:35:46,546 --> 01:35:50,425
This is traffic control. Proceed
on vector five-niner-two-two-seven.

1215
01:35:52,466 --> 01:35:54,104
I think you should know...

1216
01:35:55,306 --> 01:35:57,501
your friend Rico
is back there.

1217
01:36:06,386 --> 01:36:09,981
Get on the com and tell Fleet
to glass that rock.

1218
01:36:10,066 --> 01:36:11,704
On whose authority,
Corporal?

1219
01:36:11,786 --> 01:36:14,744
That would be mine, sir.
I assumed command of the mission.

1220
01:36:16,106 --> 01:36:18,461
Rodger Young,
we have an official request...

1221
01:36:18,546 --> 01:36:21,538
by the Mobile Infantry
to commence bombardment of Planet P.

1222
01:36:22,826 --> 01:36:25,135
I thought you were dead.

1223
01:36:25,226 --> 01:36:28,184
I'm not, but a lot
of my troopers are.

1224
01:36:28,266 --> 01:36:30,143
Negative on your request,
DeRuyter.

1225
01:36:30,226 --> 01:36:32,342
The Sky Marshal has
other plans for Planet P.

1226
01:36:32,426 --> 01:36:33,620
Welcome back.

1227
01:36:33,706 --> 01:36:36,664
MI does the dying.
Fleet just does the flying.

1228
01:36:36,746 --> 01:36:38,577
Hold on.
Something's up.

1229
01:36:38,666 --> 01:36:41,055
Fleet's mobilized
for a big operation.

1230
01:38:14,406 --> 01:38:16,158
Attention on deck!

1231
01:38:22,966 --> 01:38:24,797
Once somebody asked me...

1232
01:38:24,886 --> 01:38:27,195
if I knew the difference
between a citizen...

1233
01:38:27,286 --> 01:38:29,117
and a civilian.

1234
01:38:29,206 --> 01:38:30,719
I can tell you now.

1235
01:38:30,806 --> 01:38:32,797
A citizen has the courage...

1236
01:38:32,886 --> 01:38:37,198
to make the safety of the human race
their personal responsibility.

1237
01:38:41,206 --> 01:38:43,515
Dizzy was my friend.

1238
01:38:43,606 --> 01:38:45,642
She was a soldier.

1239
01:38:45,726 --> 01:38:47,523
But more than that...

1240
01:38:47,606 --> 01:38:49,915
she was a citizen
of the Federation.

1241
01:38:52,246 --> 01:38:54,077
Present arms!

1242
01:39:11,846 --> 01:39:14,519
Order arms!

1243
01:39:17,766 --> 01:39:19,438
Left face!

1244
01:39:32,966 --> 01:39:34,957
- Officer on deck!
- Carry on.

1245
01:39:36,486 --> 01:39:39,080
Burial detail dismissed.

1246
01:39:45,766 --> 01:39:47,916
At ease.

1247
01:39:48,006 --> 01:39:51,123
- How are you, Carl?
- Carmen, good.

1248
01:39:51,206 --> 01:39:54,004
Johnny, I'm sorry it had
to be your unit on P.

1249
01:39:54,086 --> 01:39:56,441
That mission had a very low
survival probability.

1250
01:39:56,526 --> 01:39:58,482
The bugs laid a trap
for us, didn't they?

1251
01:39:59,846 --> 01:40:02,155
Elegant proof
of intelligence, isn't it?

1252
01:40:02,246 --> 01:40:04,601
We thought there might be
a Brain Bug on P.

1253
01:40:04,686 --> 01:40:06,517
You knew, and you
sent them anyway?

1254
01:40:06,606 --> 01:40:09,837
We couldn't afford to launch an
operation if there wasn't one.

1255
01:40:11,686 --> 01:40:14,962
You don't approve.
Well, too bad.

1256
01:40:15,046 --> 01:40:16,877
We're in this for the species,
boys and girls.

1257
01:40:16,966 --> 01:40:19,241
It's simple numbers.
They have more.

1258
01:40:19,326 --> 01:40:20,998
And every day I have
to make decisions...

1259
01:40:21,086 --> 01:40:23,805
that send hundreds of people
like you to their deaths.

1260
01:40:23,886 --> 01:40:26,161
Didn't they tell you,
Colonel?

1261
01:40:26,246 --> 01:40:28,476
That's what the Mobile
Infantry is good for.

1262
01:40:28,566 --> 01:40:31,239
I hope you're ready for more.

1263
01:40:31,326 --> 01:40:34,477
We're going back to P
to capture that Brain.

1264
01:40:36,446 --> 01:40:39,085
The Roughnecks
are always ready, sir.

1265
01:40:39,166 --> 01:40:41,680
I hear they need a new lieutenant.
Want the job?

1266
01:40:41,766 --> 01:40:45,600
I'll take it, till I get killed
or you find someone better.

1267
01:40:47,726 --> 01:40:50,763
Attention. All personnel
report to your stations.

1268
01:40:50,846 --> 01:40:54,122
- Well--
- Prepare for drop in 7 5 minutes.

1269
01:40:54,206 --> 01:40:55,924
Take care of yourself,Johnny.

1270
01:40:56,006 --> 01:40:57,724
I'll see you again.

1271
01:41:10,366 --> 01:41:11,958
Officer on deck!

1272
01:41:28,686 --> 01:41:32,122
- Who are all these kids?
- We got reinforced.

1273
01:41:32,206 --> 01:41:34,322
Most of them are
fresh out of boot.

1274
01:41:34,406 --> 01:41:36,158
We're the old men, Ace.

1275
01:41:38,446 --> 01:41:40,596
This is for all you new people.

1276
01:41:40,686 --> 01:41:42,836
I only have one rule:

1277
01:41:42,926 --> 01:41:45,884
Everyone fights.
No one quits.

1278
01:41:45,966 --> 01:41:48,924
If you don't do your job,
I'll kill you myself.

1279
01:41:49,006 --> 01:41:50,234
Do you get me?

1280
01:41:50,326 --> 01:41:52,282
We get you, sir!

1281
01:41:52,366 --> 01:41:56,837
- Welcome to the Roughnecks.
- Rico's Roughnecks!

1282
01:41:59,366 --> 01:42:01,834
Today we're gonna pay
a visit to Bug City.

1283
01:42:01,926 --> 01:42:05,077
We're lookin' for a bug
no one's ever seen before.

1284
01:42:05,166 --> 01:42:06,918
Some kind of smart bug.

1285
01:42:12,606 --> 01:42:14,483
And it probably knows
we're comin'.

1286
01:42:14,566 --> 01:42:18,320
- Saddle up!
- Saddle up now!

1287
01:42:18,406 --> 01:42:20,203
Come on!
Run, run, run, run, run!

1288
01:42:31,206 --> 01:42:33,083
Evasive action.

1289
01:42:55,486 --> 01:42:57,204
Get us clear for warp,
Number Two.

1290
01:42:57,286 --> 01:42:59,595
Clear in five, four...

1291
01:42:59,686 --> 01:43:01,563
- Initiating star drive...
- three--
- in five.

1292
01:43:24,766 --> 01:43:27,075
This is Rodger Young. We're going down
Repeat, this is Rodger Young.

1293
01:43:27,166 --> 01:43:30,442
- Get out!
- We're going down.
- Abandon ship! Come on!

1294
01:43:31,806 --> 01:43:33,797
Carmen! Oh!

1295
01:43:33,886 --> 01:43:36,525
- Zander!
- Here!

1296
01:43:36,606 --> 01:43:39,598
- We've got to get to the rescue deck!
- Come on!

1297
01:43:55,486 --> 01:43:56,760
Captain!

1298
01:43:59,646 --> 01:44:02,365
Abandon ship.
That's an--

1299
01:44:03,806 --> 01:44:06,274
She's dead, Carmen.
She's dead!

1300
01:44:22,926 --> 01:44:25,645
Go! Here!

1301
01:44:40,446 --> 01:44:41,765
Follow me!

1302
01:44:53,006 --> 01:44:54,121
Ready?

1303
01:45:00,326 --> 01:45:01,645
Hit it!

1304
01:45:18,526 --> 01:45:21,199
Life pod Bravo 6-3,
two aboard.

1305
01:45:28,526 --> 01:45:32,997
Scanning for a landing zone!
Checking terrain. Here!

1306
01:45:33,086 --> 01:45:35,077
- Can you handle that?
- Piece of cake.

1307
01:45:38,726 --> 01:45:41,160
- We've lost the Rodger Young!
- What is your position?

1308
01:45:41,246 --> 01:45:44,682
Flight Command, we have confirmation.
The Rodger Young is down.

1309
01:45:44,766 --> 01:45:46,438
- Oh.Johnny!
- This is Flight Command.

1310
01:45:46,526 --> 01:45:48,517
Please repeat.
Please repeat.

1311
01:45:48,606 --> 01:45:52,042
-Johnny!
- We now have confirmation.
Rodger Young is down.

1312
01:45:52,126 --> 01:45:54,003
- I repeat, Rodger Young is down.
- Rodger Young just burned up.

1313
01:45:54,086 --> 01:45:57,317
- It's on the rescue net.
- Life pod Bravo 6-3, two aboard.

1314
01:45:57,406 --> 01:46:00,204
- Is anyone receiving?
- Any survivors?
- Is anyone receiving?

1315
01:46:00,286 --> 01:46:02,800
- Well, they're getting tarred
up there pretty bad.
- Life pod...

1316
01:46:02,886 --> 01:46:04,205
Bravo 6-3, two aboard.

1317
01:46:04,286 --> 01:46:05,799
Is anyone receiving?

1318
01:46:05,886 --> 01:46:07,205
- Is anyone receiving?
- Affirmative.

1319
01:46:07,286 --> 01:46:08,719
This is Roughneck 2-0.

1320
01:46:08,806 --> 01:46:10,285
You're breaking up.
Say again.

1321
01:46:10,366 --> 01:46:12,641
- Carmen?
- Say again. I'm losing you.

1322
01:46:12,726 --> 01:46:14,000
Carmen!

1323
01:46:17,766 --> 01:46:19,085
Prepare for landing.

1324
01:46:19,166 --> 01:46:20,918
Retros in three...

1325
01:46:21,006 --> 01:46:23,395
two, one, fire!

1326
01:46:38,806 --> 01:46:40,524
Carmen. Carmen.

1327
01:46:40,606 --> 01:46:42,676
- Hey, are you okay?
- Uh-huh.

1328
01:46:42,766 --> 01:46:44,119
Get out.
Get out.

1329
01:46:53,366 --> 01:46:57,325
This is Roughneck 2-0. Are you
receiving? Over. This is Roughneck 2-0.

1330
01:46:57,406 --> 01:47:00,716
- Carmen, are you receiving?
-Johnny, is that you?
- Yeah!

1331
01:47:00,806 --> 01:47:03,400
- It's me! Wh-What's your
position and situation?
- Yeah.

1332
01:47:03,486 --> 01:47:05,044
We're in Bug City,
20 metres underground.

1333
01:47:05,126 --> 01:47:08,243
Position:
south 42, east 118.

1334
01:47:08,326 --> 01:47:10,282
Situation is--

1335
01:47:10,366 --> 01:47:12,084
I repeat.
South 4 2, east 118.

1336
01:47:12,166 --> 01:47:14,475
What's your situation?
Over.

1337
01:47:14,566 --> 01:47:15,885
Carmen.

1338
01:47:18,046 --> 01:47:19,877
Situation is
extremely hostile.

1339
01:47:24,606 --> 01:47:26,483
I need a squad
to pull 'em out!

1340
01:47:26,566 --> 01:47:28,682
- Direction?
- Three clicks, south by southwest.

1341
01:47:34,886 --> 01:47:36,524
Look out!

1342
01:47:54,686 --> 01:47:57,075
- What do you wanna do?
- You heard the lieutenant.

1343
01:47:57,166 --> 01:48:01,318
Rescue party!
Third squad, come with me!

1344
01:48:01,406 --> 01:48:03,715
Cancel that!

1345
01:48:03,806 --> 01:48:06,445
You know as well as I do,
she's already dead.

1346
01:48:09,726 --> 01:48:11,000
Sorry, buddy.

1347
01:48:12,926 --> 01:48:16,362
Roughnecks, let's move.

1348
01:48:16,446 --> 01:48:18,437
All right.

1349
01:48:32,606 --> 01:48:34,437
Why didn't they kill us?

1350
01:48:34,526 --> 01:48:36,596
They want us alive.

1351
01:49:28,366 --> 01:49:30,596
We should go this way.

1352
01:49:31,886 --> 01:49:34,195
A Company's that way.

1353
01:49:34,286 --> 01:49:38,359
Yeah, but Carmen's
down there.

1354
01:49:38,446 --> 01:49:41,643
Hey, I hate to be rude, buddy,
but word has it she's dead.

1355
01:49:43,086 --> 01:49:44,280
She's still alive.

1356
01:49:44,366 --> 01:49:46,516
How do you know?

1357
01:49:46,606 --> 01:49:49,200
- I don't know how I know, but I know.
- Listen.

1358
01:49:49,286 --> 01:49:51,595
You got command,
but going off mission--

1359
01:49:51,686 --> 01:49:53,961
- That's a serious offence.
- Yeah.

1360
01:49:54,046 --> 01:49:55,923
I think they
hang you for that.

1361
01:49:58,046 --> 01:50:01,721
Roughneck 2-0,
proceed on mission.

1362
01:50:01,806 --> 01:50:04,320
I need two volunteers.

1363
01:51:12,246 --> 01:51:13,679
One day...

1364
01:51:13,766 --> 01:51:16,075
someone like me...

1365
01:51:16,166 --> 01:51:17,838
is gonna kill you...

1366
01:51:17,926 --> 01:51:19,962
and your whole fucking race.

1367
01:52:16,606 --> 01:52:17,721
You know what this is?

1368
01:52:20,606 --> 01:52:21,880
Sure you do.

1369
01:52:23,406 --> 01:52:25,874
You're some kind
of big, fat, smart bug...

1370
01:52:25,966 --> 01:52:27,240
aren't you?

1371
01:52:29,366 --> 01:52:31,277
Come on.

1372
01:52:42,206 --> 01:52:43,924
This is Roughneck 2-0.

1373
01:52:44,006 --> 01:52:47,476
Brain Bug sighted moving
west of grid five.

1374
01:52:49,646 --> 01:52:50,999
Run!

1375
01:53:19,886 --> 01:53:22,241
Go! Go!

1376
01:53:22,326 --> 01:53:25,636
- Give me the nuke!
- You trying to be a hero, Watkins?

1377
01:53:27,726 --> 01:53:30,957
I'm trying to kill
some bugs, sir!

1378
01:53:31,046 --> 01:53:34,083
Get outta here!
Get outta here!

1379
01:53:35,566 --> 01:53:36,840
Move!

1380
01:53:41,326 --> 01:53:44,443
Come on! You like that?
You like that? Come on!

1381
01:53:44,526 --> 01:53:45,800
You want a little more?

1382
01:53:49,086 --> 01:53:52,044
You like that? You like that?
You like that? You like that?
You want a little more?

1383
01:53:58,006 --> 01:53:59,155
Come on! Come on!

1384
01:54:04,286 --> 01:54:05,560
Come on, come on, come on!

1385
01:54:29,086 --> 01:54:30,235
Come on, Carmen.

1386
01:54:42,046 --> 01:54:44,480
- We did it!
- We won!

1387
01:54:49,566 --> 01:54:51,716
- What's going on?
- They got it!

1388
01:54:51,806 --> 01:54:52,921
Come on!

1389
01:55:05,846 --> 01:55:09,759
Pull! Pull! Pull!

1390
01:55:25,606 --> 01:55:27,517
Quiet!

1391
01:55:38,606 --> 01:55:40,756
What's it thinking, Colonel?

1392
01:55:58,086 --> 01:55:59,314
It's afraid.

1393
01:56:00,726 --> 01:56:01,954
It's afraid!

1394
01:56:05,886 --> 01:56:09,117
- Come on.
- Yeah!

1395
01:56:09,206 --> 01:56:11,515
Carl! Carl! Hey!

1396
01:56:15,206 --> 01:56:18,004
Well, look who's here.
You made it. Good.

1397
01:56:18,086 --> 01:56:21,237
It was you, wasn't it?
You told me how to find Carmen.

1398
01:56:27,526 --> 01:56:28,959
Well, that's classified.

1399
01:56:34,806 --> 01:56:37,445
You know, whenever
the three of us are together...

1400
01:56:37,526 --> 01:56:40,324
I feel like things
might just work out.

1401
01:56:40,406 --> 01:56:42,237
I hope you're right,
Carmen.

1402
01:56:42,326 --> 01:56:45,124
We've got one of their Brains now.
Pretty soon we'll know how they think.

1403
01:56:45,206 --> 01:56:47,674
And then we'll know
how to beat them.

1404
01:56:47,766 --> 01:56:49,757
One day it will all be over...

1405
01:56:49,846 --> 01:56:52,644
and everyone will forget
that this was the moment.

1406
01:56:52,726 --> 01:56:55,524
This is when it turned.

1407
01:56:55,606 --> 01:56:59,519
And it wasn't the mighty Fleet,
it wasn't some fancy new weapon.

1408
01:57:03,286 --> 01:57:06,244
It was a drill instructor named Zim
who captured a Brain.

1409
01:57:06,326 --> 01:57:07,839
Come on!
Who am I?

1410
01:57:07,926 --> 01:57:09,962
- Yeah!
- Zim?

1411
01:57:11,326 --> 01:57:13,556
He got him! Yeah!

1412
01:57:13,646 --> 01:57:15,796
Zim. Zim got the bug.

1413
01:57:15,886 --> 01:57:17,399
Zim got the bug, man!

1414
01:57:17,486 --> 01:57:20,637
- Good job, Sergeant.
- Thank you, sir.

1415
01:57:20,726 --> 01:57:25,356
- That would be private, sir.
- Carry on, Private.

1416
01:57:25,446 --> 01:57:27,960
- Yes, sir!
- Yeah!

1417
01:57:32,206 --> 01:57:35,164
What mysteries
will the Brain Bug reveal?

1418
01:57:35,246 --> 01:57:39,956
Federal scientists are working
around the clock to probe its secrets.

1419
01:57:40,046 --> 01:57:43,402
Once we understand the bug,
we will defeat it.

1420
01:57:54,326 --> 01:57:55,759
We have the ships.

1421
01:57:55,846 --> 01:57:57,120
We have the weapons.

1422
01:57:58,566 --> 01:58:00,477
We need soldiers.

1423
01:58:00,566 --> 01:58:02,716
Soldiers like
Lieutenant Stack Lumbrezer.

1424
01:58:02,806 --> 01:58:04,797
We're over the target
area now, Captain.

1425
01:58:04,886 --> 01:58:07,923
-And Captain Carmen Ibanez.
- This is the captain speaking.

1426
01:58:08,006 --> 01:58:09,598
All personnel
prepare for drop.

1427
01:58:09,686 --> 01:58:12,325
Soldiers like Private Ace Levy
and Lieutenant John Rico.

1428
01:58:12,406 --> 01:58:15,762
Come on, you apes!
You wanna live forever?

1429
01:58:15,846 --> 01:58:17,245
We need you all.

1430
01:58:17,326 --> 01:58:20,636
Service guarantees citizenship.
